window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["11"]={"https://theconversation.com/el-nino-is-nudging-the-pacifics-cyclone-risk-east-what-does-that-mean-for-new-zealand-296680":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"8fd9a536e654047d0fd14d64b908bff7409ea462348e8b0d77fa0b8a334aa9c0","read":"https://theconversation.com/el-nino-is-nudging-the-pacifics-cyclone-risk-east-what-does-that-mean-for-new-zealand-296680","bytes":185306,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"El Niño is nudging the Pacific’s cyclone risk east. What does that mean for New Zealand?","by":[{"n":"James Renwick","r":"Professor of Physical Geography (Climate Science), Te Herenga Waka — Victoria University of Wellington"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T17:44:28Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Tropical Cyclone Xavier, ",["which has strengthened","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/pacific/2620097/tropical-cyclone-xavier-to-bring-damaging-winds-to-northern-cook-islands"]," while moving near parts of the northern Cook Islands, reminds us that cyclone season is now underway in the Southwest Pacific."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the system’s location, east of where many Pacific cyclones typically develop, also hints at how this season could look different to others."]},{"k":"p","s":["With ",["a powerful El Niño","https://theconversation.com/el-nino-threatens-health-too-early-warnings-done-right-can-save-lives-295379"]," taking hold, scientists expect cyclone activity to shift further east, exposing some island communities to greater risk while reducing it elsewhere. So, what does this mean for New Zealand?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Why cyclone risk is shifting east"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tropical cyclones are ",["enormous, rotating storms","https://niwa.co.nz/climate-and-weather/climate-present-and-past/southwest-pacific-climate/tropical-cyclones"]," that develop over warm oceans. Like ",["giant atmospheric heat engines","https://media.bom.gov.au/social/blog/46/a-look-inside-the-structure-of-a-tropical-cyclone/"],", they draw heat and moisture from the sea, releasing energy as water vapour condenses into clouds and rain. This fuels powerful winds, torrential downpours and sometimes devastating storm surges."]},{"k":"p","s":["They typically form in the Southwest Pacific between November and April. This season, Earth Sciences New Zealand ",["anticipates","https://niwa.co.nz/climate-and-weather/southwest-pacific-tropical-cyclone-outlook/southwest-pacific-tropical-cyclone-outlook-october-2026"]," seven to 11 named cyclones, compared with a long-term average of nine. At least four could become severe, reaching ",["category 3 or higher","https://www.noaa.gov/jetstream/tropical/tropical-cyclone-introduction/tropical-cyclone-classification"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the more interesting part of the forecast is geographical. While normal to reduced activity is expected in the western Southwest Pacific, risk is elevated near and east of the ",["International Date Line","https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/international-date-line.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of this comes down to ",["El Niño","https://niwa.co.nz/news/el-nino-2026-what-you-need-know"],", when unusually warm waters develop across the central and eastern equatorial Pacific, accompanied by changes in atmospheric circulation and rainfall."]},{"k":"p","s":["One important feature is the ",["South Pacific Convergence Zone","https://niwa.co.nz/climate-and-weather/climate-present-and-past/southwest-pacific-climate/south-pacific-convergence-zone"]," (SPCZ), a broad band of cloud and rainfall stretching from around Papua New Guinea towards French Polynesia. It helps determine where cyclones form and travel. During El Niño, the SPCZ tends to shift northeastwards, towards the equator."]},{"k":"p","s":["Think of this as opening a door. As the convergence zone shifts, cyclones can develop and travel farther east, increasing the exposure of islands in the central and eastern Pacific, including French Polynesia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, the Coral Sea, traditionally ",["a major cyclone breeding ground","https://www.bom.gov.au/climate/about/?bookmark=tc"],", can experience reduced activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["During La Niña, the opposite phase of the ",["El Niño-Southern Oscillation","https://niwa.co.nz/climate-and-weather/climate-present-and-past/southwest-pacific-climate/el-nino-southern-oscillation"]," (ENSO), warmer waters and favourable conditions tend to be concentrated farther west, shifting cyclone activity towards the western Pacific."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why New Zealand is different"]},{"k":"p","s":["Given the strength of the current El Niño, we might expect New Zealand’s cyclone risk to change too. Yet it’s been placed at near normal this season."]},{"k":"p","s":["On average, at least one ex-tropical cyclone passes within 550km of New Zealand each year. Some seasons bring none, others several. That’s because getting a cyclone here requires several atmospheric ingredients to come together."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, the storm needs to be in the right place. In the tropics, cyclones generally move westwards, carried by the trade winds. But as they move south, they encounter the prevailing westerlies and typically curve eastwards."]},{"k":"p","s":["If that turn happens too far east, near the International Date Line, the cyclone will likely miss New Zealand. To reach Aotearoa, it generally needs to begin that turn further west, somewhere between Australia and Fiji."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then the mid-latitude atmosphere needs to cooperate. A trough or low-pressure system moving through from the Southern Ocean can interact with the cyclone, potentially reinvigorating it."]},{"k":"p","s":["The westerlies must also be strong enough to steer the storm towards New Zealand, but not so strong that they rapidly sweep it eastwards. As cyclones leave the tropics, they undergo ",["extratropical transition","https://about.metservice.com/learning/tropical-cyclones-extra-tropical-transition"],", becoming a different type of weather system. But that doesn’t necessarily make them harmless."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some of New Zealand’s most damaging storms, including ",["Bola","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclone_Bola"]," in 1988 and ",["Gabrielle","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclone_Gabrielle"]," in 2023, involved these transformed systems."]},{"k":"p","s":["I sometimes compare the process to a pinball machine. A cyclone reaches the edge of the tropics like a ball poised at the top of the chute. A small change in atmospheric circulation can send it in a completely different direction."]},{"k":"p","s":["This makes seasonal predictions difficult. Even when scientists examine past years with similar conditions, known as ",["analogue years","https://niwa.co.nz/images/analog-seasons-and-intensity-tropical-cyclones-and-storms-occurred-southwest-pacific"],", no two seasons are identical."]},{"k":"h","s":["What about climate change?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although warmer oceans and air can provide more energy and moisture for cyclones, that doesn’t necessarily mean more storms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Research generally points towards ",["fewer tropical cyclones globally","https://www.csiro.au/en/research/environmental-impacts/climate-change/State-of-the-Climate/Future-climate"],", but ",["a greater proportion reaching high intensities","https://www.gfdl.noaa.gov/global-warming-and-hurricanes/"],", with heavier rainfall and potentially more destructive impacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["The relationship ",["between climate change and El Niño and La Niña","https://earthathome.org/quick-faqs/el-nino-and-climate-change/"]," is less straightforward."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Evidence suggests","https://research.noaa.gov/new-research-volume-explores-future-of-enso-under-influence-of-climate-change/"]," the rainfall extremes associated with these events are intensifying. Regions that become wetter during El Niño can experience heavier rainfall, while areas prone to drying can face more severe droughts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Very strong El Niño events could also become more frequent as the planet warms, although questions remain about how climate change will alter ENSO’s overall behaviour."]},{"k":"p","s":["For New Zealand, a near-normal cyclone outlook shouldn’t be mistaken for low risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earth Sciences New Zealand expects the likelihood of an ex-tropical cyclone affecting New Zealand to be greater in late summer and autumn than before Christmas, with northern and western areas potentially more exposed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Historically, February and March have been particularly active months for systems approaching New Zealand. But cyclones can develop quickly, and even a weakening storm can bring damaging winds, heavy rain and dangerous seas."]},{"k":"p","s":["So, whether people are heading away for a summer holiday or camping by the coast, it’s worth keeping an eye on the forecast. As Xavier is reminding communities in the northern Cook Islands, cyclone season is here."]}],"chars":5739},"https://theconversation.com/wartime-memory-shows-the-china-russia-partnership-is-anything-but-limitless-293877":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"c65e72814ca5a4df74d5c1b1c5e1c3e66990fef1aeb8135754bc2d021c7d2477","read":"https://theconversation.com/wartime-memory-shows-the-china-russia-partnership-is-anything-but-limitless-293877","bytes":186345,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Wartime memory shows the China-Russia partnership is anything but ‘limitless’","by":[{"n":"Vincent K.L. Chang","r":"Assistant Professor of the History and International Relations of Modern China, Leiden University"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T17:42:18Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["For more than a decade, China and Russia have sought to align their official memories of the second world war. They have staged prominent joint commemorations and military parades, while also coordinating remembrance dates and harmonising ",["their official discourses","https://leidenasiacentre.nl/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/23-10-30-Shared-Histories-Distinct-Memories.pdf"]," about the war."]},{"k":"p","s":["The latest example of this “memory alliance” came in September when the ",["Chinese","https://theconversation.com/topics/china-336"]," and ",["Russian","https://theconversation.com/topics/russia-1376"]," ambassadors to New Zealand, Wang Xiaolong and Stanislav Krans, published a ",["joint opinion article","https://newzealand.mid.ru/en/press_center/news/article_by_his_excellencies_mr_stanislav_krans_and_mr_wang_xiaolong_ambassadors_of_russia_and_china_"]," in the NZ Herald to mark the 81st anniversary of the war’s end."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their article insisted the lessons of the war must not be forgotten. They said this entails safeguarding the UN‑centred international order and rejecting historical revisionism that downplays Chinese and Russian sacrifices or glosses over Nazi and fascist atrocities."]},{"k":"p","s":["China and Russia’s ",["memory alliance","https://thediplomat.com/2022/09/shifting-world-war-ii-memory-in-east-asia-signals-newly-emerging-global-alliances"]," serves two main purposes. First, it deepens the supposedly ",["“limitless”","https://www.reuters.com/world/china/moscow-beijing-partnership-has-no-limits-2022-02-04/"]," partnership between the two countries. Second, it forms the basis for them to defend what they regard as the foundations of the post‑war global order."]},{"k":"p","s":["In their view, the core principles of the global order that emerged from the second world war are multilateralism, sovereignty and non‑interference in other countries’ internal affairs. They claim these hard-won gains ",["are being undermined","https://www.9dashline.com/article/victory-and-sacrifice-the-dual-message-behind-chinas-commemorations"]," by what they portray as US‑led western arrogance, aggression and unilateralism."]},{"k":"p","s":["For Beijing, this perceived subversion has taken the form of semiconductor export bans, tariffs on Chinese EVs, efforts to contain China’s influence in the Indo-Pacific and Japan’s growing military role in the region. China also views western support for Taiwan, which reverted to Chinese control after Japan’s defeat in 1945, as a violation of the post-war order."]},{"k":"p","s":["For Moscow, the threat comes from Nato’s enlargement, perceived western interference in Ukraine culminating in President Viktor Yanukovych’s ousting in 2014 and the global sanctions regime imposed after the full-scale invasion of Ukraine. Russian leaders ",["accuse the west","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/vladimir-putin-russia-respects-us-world-superpower/"]," of disregarding Russia’s “legitimate interests” and security concerns."]},{"k":"p","s":["Invoking the “scourge” of the second world war enables both Russia and China to frame these concerns while ",["advocating","https://thediplomat.com/2025/08/chinas-victory-day-message-points-to-struggle-ahead"]," a multipolar world defined by regional spheres of influence. Yet, as ",["my research shows","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/modern-asian-studies/article/allies-apart-china-russia-and-the-limits-of-mnemonic-friendship/3EBBC14A85DC69F59FE627751AA7E06B"],", three trends in Russia and China’s official war remembrance reveal strains in their ",["proclaimed no-limits partnership","https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/china-defends-limitless-partnership-with-russia"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["A limited partnership"]},{"k":"p","s":["First, there is ",["little convergence","https://thediplomat.com/2023/09/what-world-war-ii-narratives-reveal-about-china-russia-relations"]," in their historical narratives on key episodes of the war or on the nature of their wartime relationship. Both sides advance different claims about who contributed most to defeating Japan and who assisted whom."]},{"k":"p","s":["Russian narratives emphasise the Red Army’s decisive contribution, downplaying China’s role in tying down Japanese forces. Beijing, meanwhile, suggests it made ",["the largest sacrifice","https://doi.org/10.1093/ia/iiac021"]," among the allies. It claims to have been decisive in prolonging Japan’s entanglement in China and securing its ultimate defeat."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2023, I carried out an ",["analysis","https://leidenasiacentre.nl/publication-shared-histories-distinct-memories"]," of more than 14,000 Chinese and Russian state-sponsored news articles with my colleague Eric Zhang. Combined with extensive fieldwork in China, our findings suggest that convergence with Russia’s preferred historical narratives has been limited to shared silences about episodes that would embarrass each other."]},{"k":"p","s":["These include wartime mutual frictions or Soviet crimes during the liberation of north-eastern China."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even more striking, given the strategic importance both sides attach to their friendship, is how little they have made of personal wartime stories. This is despite the ",["rich historical material","https://doi.org/10.1017/S0026749X26102091"]," available for constructing a shared memory."]},{"k":"p","s":["Roughly 1,500 Soviet advisers and 2,000 combat pilots supported China’s early war effort. About 200 of these so-called “Flying Eagles” were killed. Yet their stories remain largely unknown to the public, with only a few of these aviators commemorated in China."]},{"k":"p","s":["One exception is Hryhorij Kulishenko, a Ukrainian-born Soviet Air Force pilot who was killed during the battle for Wuhan in October 1939. During a 2013 state visit to Russia, Chinese leader Xi Jinping highlighted Kulishenko’s story as a symbol of enduring solidarity between the two countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Addressing the Moscow State Institute of International Relations, Xi ",["described","https://www.mfa.gov.cn/eng/xw/zyjh/202405/t20240530_11340559.html"]," Kulishenko as a hero who had fought “side by side with the Chinese people” and would never be forgotten. But in recent years, these “Flying Eagles” have gradually faded from China’s official narrative of friendship with Russia."]},{"k":"p","s":["By contrast, Chinese official accounts and history exhibitions are replete with references to Sino‑US cooperation during the war, especially the American volunteer group of the Chinese Air Force known as the “Flying Tigers”. They ",["have been portrayed","https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202508/30/WS68b25886a3108622abc9df14_4.html"]," by Chinese state media as a lasting symbol of shared struggle and friendship."]},{"k":"p","s":["This leads to the second trend: the China-Russia memory alliance is being diluted by Beijing’s increasingly active memory diplomacy toward the US."]},{"k":"p","s":["China’s efforts to highlight its wartime cooperation with the US reached a peak during Xi’s recent state visit to Washington. At the White House welcome ceremony, Donald Trump echoed Xi’s praise for the Flying Tigers. He even ",["recalled","https://youtu.be/7VX53SrzyZM?si=Gg58YFgBFgQSTciR&t=370"]," that the US and China had fought together as “allies” during the war."]},{"k":"p","s":["The third trend is the recent emergence of Ukraine in China’s second world war commemorations."]},{"k":"p","s":["In September 2025, on the 80th anniversary of Victory Day, the Chinese embassy in Kyiv ",["donated","https://english.news.cn/20250918/420790091594409abc15e89028b01cd7/c.html"]," a bronze statue of Kulishenko – the very pilot Xi had praised in Moscow in 2013 as a symbol of China-Russia friendship – to a memorial in Cherepyn, his birthplace."]},{"k":"p","s":["This gesture reflects a subtle but significant shift in how China frames the memory of this ",["celebrated Soviet hero","https://www.xinhuanet.com/english/2019-12/13/c_138629419.htm"],", moving from his earlier mobilisation for Chinese-Russian friendship towards a Sino‑Ukrainian narrative."]},{"k":"p","s":["In China, official war memory is closely tied to policy direction. After more than a decade of cultivating a “no‑limits” friendship with Moscow, this latest adjustment of wartime remembrance may reveal Beijing’s unease with being perceived as aligned too closely with Russia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Partnering with Russia may help Beijing selectively uphold and revive certain elements of the post‑war global order. But China is simultaneously signalling that it seeks continued cooperation with the west and does not wish to become alienated or isolated."]}],"chars":6396},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/djibouti":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"860e14d88750d92f1ebac417506b1e123b2ff03df7e8f19b1c4dd9bcc760cfa9","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/djibouti","bytes":47917,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Djibouti travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-04T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-07-27T15:03:02+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Djibouti-Eritrea border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Djibouti-Eritrea border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/djibouti/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Djibouti’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Djibouti set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Djibouti Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Djibouti, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Djibouti."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can buy a tourist visa when you arrive in Djibouti with payment in cash in US dollars. You can also apply for a visa online before travelling or contact the ",["Djibouti Embassy","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],". You must have evidence of your onward journey."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Djibouti, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Djibouti guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/65/djibouti#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Djibouti. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has ",["safety advice for regions of Djibouti","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/djibouti/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Djibouti"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Djibouti."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorism attacks could be indiscriminate, including in crowded areas and places frequented by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels, restaurants and bars"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious events"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting events"]},{"k":"li","s":["military bases"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The terrorist group Al Shabaab may see Djibouti and international interests within Djibouti as legitimate targets. This is because Djibouti participates in the African Union peacekeeping mission, ATMIS, and joins in international support of the Somali government. Al Shabaab has issued public threats against Djibouti."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of petty crime. Take precautions such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not walking alone late at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping valuables, particularly cameras and passports, out of sight"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts. You should show respect to those who are fasting and take care not to offend local values."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that government offices and public institutions may change their working hours during Ramadan"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit and debit cards are not widely accepted. If credit cards are accepted, you often need a Visa card. ATMs are normally available in Djibouti City, but they may not accept Mastercard. Make sure that you carry enough cash."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drinking alcohol is allowed, but you can get a 2-year prison sentence for drunken behaviour."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras"]},{"k":"p","s":["Photographing infrastructure, such as ports, public buildings, airports, military facilities, and bridges, is prohibited. Your equipment could be confiscated, and you could be arrested. When taking photos near prohibited places, take care and seek local advice if you are unsure."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual behaviour is not illegal but is not common in Djiboutian public life. Same-sex couples showing affection in public could attract the attention of the authorities under laws around “good morals”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Djibouti, see information on ",["driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Djibouti for up to 12 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or obtain a local Djiboutian driving licence through the Ministry of Interior."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are generally poor. Many drivers use the legal narcotic khat, which contributes to speeding and unsafe driving. Roads are often narrow and poorly lit and maintained."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay on paved roads and avoid travelling outside city centres after dark. Vehicles often have no lights and livestock may be on the roads. Many large trucks use the main Djibouti-Ethiopia road."]},{"k":"p","s":["On some major roads police use wire coils as roadblocks, which are not clearly visible at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list"]," (ASL) lists all known airlines in Djibouti that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a significant risk of piracy and armed robbery in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean. Pirates continue to attack fishing dhows around the Horn of Africa. International naval counter-piracy forces advise all sailing yachts to avoid the designated high-risk area where there is risk of hijacking. See ",["piracy and armed robbery at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Intense rainfall is rare but can cause flash floods, particularly around Djibouti City. Flash floods can cause:"]},{"k":"li","s":["major disruption to travel and infrastructure, including schools and public places"]},{"k":"li","s":["damage to buildings and roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["water-borne and respiratory disease outbreaks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay away from flood areas and follow official advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes and volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes and volcanic eruptions are a risk in Djibouti. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Djibouti. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/djibouti"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/djibouti/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Military activity in the Red Sea area"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of military activity is currently underway in response to attempts by Houthi militants to prevent movement of international shipping in the Red Sea. While the area of activity is limited to the Red Sea and Yemen, there is a possibility that the situation could change at short notice. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/djibouti/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information"]},{"k":"h","s":["Djibouti-Eritrea border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Djibouti-Eritrea border."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2008 there were military clashes between Djibouti and Eritrea after Eritrean forces entered the disputed Djibouti border region. The situation remains fragile and further conflict is possible."]},{"k":"h","s":["Djibouti-Somaliland border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take great care if you travel to the Djibouti-Somaliland border. The Djiboutian military have set up roadblocks and checkpoints. Follow the advice given by the authorities and seek military approval for journeys in this area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Landmines near borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are unmarked landmines near the Djibouti-Eritrea border. In other border areas most landmines have been marked or cleared. Djibouti’s borders with Ethiopia and Somalia are not always clearly identified."]},{"k":"h","s":["Roads north of Tadjoura"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take great care travelling on roads north of Tadjoura and Obock where there are military roadblocks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Respect advice given by those operating the roadblocks. If required, get formal military approval for your journey."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 21 35 09 62 or 21 35 27 12 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Djibouti","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/65/djibouti#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Djibouti","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/65/djibouti#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosoma"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Djibouti"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in Djibouti are limited. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Djibouti","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/djibouti-list-of-funeral-directors-medical-facilities-and-translators"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Djibouti"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 21 35 09 62 or 21 35 27 12"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 18"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 17"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Djibouti"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Djibouti"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Djibouti"]," in Djibouti"]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Djibouti","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/djibouti-prisoners-pack-2015"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/djibouti/british-embassy-addis-ababa"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/djibouti/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]," *[FCDO]: Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office"]}],"chars":13360,"change":"New information about military activity in the Red Sea area ('Regional risks’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/how-groomers-operate-and-why-victims-become-trapped-296535":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"e04a285c12add47b115d64b2296783c6ce805b3f0075cc2b3a6d1fe6647a9d67","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-groomers-operate-and-why-victims-become-trapped-296535","bytes":179435,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How groomers operate – and why victims become trapped","by":[{"n":"Emily Chiang","r":"Research Associate, Aston Institute for Forensic Linguistics, Aston University"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T16:54:19Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Entertainer and children’s author David Walliams is alleged to have used his fame to approach teenage girls, in some cases reportedly initiating sexual contact with them. Walliams has ",["denied the allegations","https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/nov/11/what-is-david-walliams-accused-of"],", but the claims raise some familiar tropes about grooming: why did she go, why didn’t she say no, why didn’t she tell anyone?"]},{"k":"p","s":["After a legal battle, ITV News and ",["The Guardian","https://theconversation.com/topics/the-guardian-4836"]," have now published ",["the findings of","https://www.theguardian.com/news/video/2026/nov/10/the-allegations-against-david-walliams-investigation-by-the-guardian-and-itv-news"]," a three-year investigation into Walliams, reporting allegations that date back to 2003."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this and other cases, there will always be people who focus not on the claims, but on the young person and what they should have done differently. Linguistic research on how grooming actually works suggests that this instinct is exactly the result that grooming is designed to produce."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many people imagine sexual grooming as a recognisable and clearly staged process. Build friendship, then trust, then secrecy – all leading towards the offender’s ultimate goal of sexual gratification. But if this were the case, victims could notice the steps and walk away."]},{"k":"p","s":["Along with a colleague, I undertook ",["linguistic analysis","https://ojs.letras.up.pt/index.php/LLLD/article/view/2411"]," of real chatroom conversations between convicted offenders and adult volunteers posing as 12 to 14-year-old girls. The conversations were made public by the now defunct organisation Perverted Justice, whose activity led to the apprehension and conviction of the offenders. In our analysis, we did not find the pattern mentioned above."]},{"k":"p","s":["We identified 14 recurring “moves” – parts of the offenders’ language that have particular functions. These include building rapport (for instance by sharing personal stories), assessing risk by checking parents’ schedules or the presence of a boyfriend, escalating sexual topics and planning offline meetings. But these moves overlapped and repeated, with no typical structure emerging."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rather, offenders seemed to tailor their grooming styles, perhaps according to their individual goals and who they believed they were talking to."]},{"k":"h","s":["Trust and rapport"]},{"k":"p","s":["What was consistent was the large amount of rapport-building, which often ran through the whole interaction. Grooming research invariably shows that ",["rapport-building and trust development","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2666799125000309#bib0033"]," are the central devices used to persuade and manipulate."]},{"k":"p","s":["This may be through compliments, sharing personal information and declarations of trust. Grooming strategies are designed to develop intimacy and trust, isolate the victim and dismantle the ",["“red flags”","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0145213422005324"]," that might alert them to the manipulative nature of the conversation. Trust development makes it much harder for victims to notice devious intentions – there is no obvious point at which the young person has failed to spot something plainly visible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Offenders in our data spent much of their conversations sizing up their targets. They would try to work out whether a target was likely to engage, suited their preferences, was accessible and unlikely to expose them. We called this a “risk-reward ratio assessment” – in other words, a judgement about whether this person was worth their effort."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["another study","https://academic.oup.com/applij/article/40/4/675/4952155?login=false"],", we examined the case of an offender who took a scattergun approach, in this case targeting nearly 1,000 potential young victims. This individual would strategically cycle through an array of fake online personas to identify the one most likely to “hook” his target. The vast majority ignored or rejected his first advance, at which point they were dropped. But this is the point of the scattergun approach; a small percentage, usually the most vulnerable, will respond."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our work also revealed how offenders manage the risk of being caught. For many we studied, a key strategy was to use language that shifted responsibility on to the target."]},{"k":"p","s":["Questions were often formulated to elicit sexually explicit content by positioning the target as the one in control. The groomer might say, for example, “how far do you want to go”, “tell me what you wanna do”. This phrasing both presumes interest and makes declining more difficult, while laying the groundwork to say later that the young person had led the conversation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another feature was what we termed the “mitigating lol”. This could be something like “u should send me a nude vid lol”. This served to reduce the impact of a sexual question by implying playfulness. It also supports future claims that the requests was insincere – possibly a useful tactic in a trial. We can only infer the purpose, but it points to the same strategy of building in deniability."]},{"k":"p","s":["I cannot speak directly to the Walliams allegations, but when it comes to celebrities in general, the task of building trust and rapport may well be easier. The victims already feel they know them, and are made to feel special by being approached. It’s also easy to see how the perks of celebrity could do much of the persuasive work."]},{"k":"p","s":["A widely used ",["definition of grooming","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13552600601069414"]," across linguistics and psychology describes preparing the child, their significant adults and the wider environment for abuse. Compliance and secrecy are explicit goals. They are not evidence of the victim’s character."]},{"k":"p","s":["So when people ask, “why did they keep replying?” or “why did they go to the house?” they are asking why a technique that was designed to engage did in fact keep them engaged. When we ask, “why didn’t they tell anyone?” we are questioning why a strategy engineered to cultivate silence did exactly that."]},{"k":"p","s":["Grooming involves a complex network of strategies. But we know it is never the young person’s behaviour that’s the problem. The “perfect victim” who resists every advance and raises the alarm at every opportunity is a myth."]},{"k":"p","s":["Better understanding of the strategies can help caregivers, educators and children to recognise grooming earlier. It should also shape what we say to victims after the fact. Let’s stop asking why they gave their email address, why they went to the house, why they didn’t tell anyone. Let’s question instead the actions of those responsible."]}],"chars":5921},"https://theconversation.com/kabinet-prabowo-makin-gemuk-tapi-perwakilan-perempuan-tetap-minim-293855":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"b39debaec1eae583d49a72c9ca530afafcefa94395108bfdf2aed5c90c85aa3f","read":"https://theconversation.com/kabinet-prabowo-makin-gemuk-tapi-perwakilan-perempuan-tetap-minim-293855","bytes":179429,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Kabinet Prabowo makin gemuk, tapi perwakilan perempuan tetap minim","by":[{"n":"Rafi Aufa Mawardi","r":"Dosen dan Peneliti di Departemen Sosiologi, Fakultas Ilmu Sosial dan Ilmu Politik, Universitas Airlangga"}],"pub":"2026-10-08T09:16:19Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• ‘Reshuffle’ dan penambahan posisi pemerintahan belum diikuti peningkatan representasi perempuan."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Jaringan elite dan rekrutmen politik menghambat akses perempuan ke kekuasaan."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Representasi perempuan harus diukur dari pengaruh, bukan sekadar jumlah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sudah tujuh kali Presiden Prabowo Subianto ",["merombak kabinetnya","https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2026/10/01/13391601/prabowo-reshuffle-kabinet-menteri-dan-pejabat-merapat-ke-istana"],". Pada reshuffle terakhir 1 Oktober lalu, Prabowo melantik 10 menteri dan wakil menteri. Beberapa hari kemudian, pemerintah juga melantik ",["26 anggota Dewan Pertimbangan Presiden (Wantimpres)","https://setkab.go.id/presiden-prabowo-angkat-26-anggota-wantimpres-di-istana-negara/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perombakan tersebut memicu perdebatan tentang gemuknya struktur pemerintahan, ",["efisiensi birokrasi","https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2026/10/02/15545811/rocky-gerung-dilantik-prabowo-jadi-anggota-wantimpres"],", serta anggaran yang harus dikeluarkan negara. Tapi ada satu persoalan yang justru luput dari perhatian: keterwakilan perempuan tak bertambah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Rezim Prabowo: Politik maskulin paternalistik, kesetaraan gender hanya omon-omon","https://theconversation.com/rezim-prabowo-politik-maskulin-paternalistik-kesetaraan-gender-hanya-omon-omon-269280"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Hanya ada 12 perempuan yang menjadi menteri (4 orang) dan wakil menteri (8 orang) dari total 104 pejabat Kabinet Merah Putih. Sementara itu, dari 26 anggota Wantimpres yang baru dilantik, hanya satu perempuan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemerintahan Prabowo belum menunjukkan upaya serius untuk memperbaiki ketimpangan gender. Ketika ruang kekuasaan terus diperluas tetapi perempuan tetap tersisih, reshuffle dan pembentukan lembaga baru berisiko hanya memperbesar struktur kekuasaan tanpa membuatnya lebih representatif."]},{"k":"h","s":["Makna besar dari angka representasi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Perempuan masih menjadi minoritas dalam ruang pengambilan keputusan di tingkat eksekutif jika kita melihat proporsi perempuan di dalamnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalahnya bukan semata-mata soal jumlah perempuan, melainkan tentang siapa yang memiliki akses untuk masuk ke pusat kekuasaan dan siapa yang dianggap layak untuk berada di sana. ",["Keadilan","https://books.google.co.id/books?hl=id&lr=&id=IJxT6pxjO7YC&oi=fnd&pg=PA1&dq=nancy+fraser+recognition&ots=YSHKStGPpX&sig=iQ3vsYxBt2XX9I6LVVthsGvs_aM&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=nancy%20fraser%20recognition&f=false"]," tidak hanya menyangkut pengakuan (recognition) dan distribusi sumber daya (redistribution), melainkan juga representasi (representation)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan perspektif ini, keberadaan beberapa perempuan di kabinet belum otomatis menunjukkan pemerintahan yang inklusif apabila struktur pengambilan keputusan secara keseluruhan masih didominasi oleh laki-laki."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian tentang representasi politik","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1478-9302.2009.00185.x"]," menunjukkan keterwakilan perempuan tidak terjadi secara otomatis hanya karena perempuan memiliki pendidikan atau kemampuan memadai. Proses rekrutmen politik, jaringan elite, partai, serta aturan formal dan informal ikut menentukan siapa yang akhirnya mendapatkan jabatan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keterwakilan perempuan dalam kabinet pemerintahan di berbagai negara menunjukkan bahwa perempuan secara historis lebih sedikit masuk kabinet. Sekalipun berhasil masuk, perempuan sering ditempatkan pada bidang yang dianggap “feminin” dan kurang bergengsi."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Studi terhadap 117 negara","https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1017/S0022381612000382"]," menunjukkan bahwa akses perempuan terhadap kekuasaan kabinet dipengaruhi bukan hanya oleh jumlah perempuan dalam politik, tetapi juga proses rekrutmen dan jenis portofolio yang diberikan kepada mereka."]},{"k":"p","s":["Artinya, pemerintah tidak bisa sekadar mengatakan bahwa jabatan diberikan berdasarkan kompetensi. Kompetensi memang penting, tetapi kesempatan untuk menunjukkan kompetensi tidak pernah sepenuhnya netral."]},{"k":"h","s":["Haruskah laki-laki terus mendominasi?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Jaringan politik berperan besar dalam menentukan siapa yang masuk ke pusat kekuasaan. Masalahnya, ",["jaringan elite","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/gove.12352"]," yang bersifat tertutup dapat menjadi hambatan bagi perempuan untuk masuk ke kabinet."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alhasil, proses rekrutmennya sangat bergantung pada kepercayaan dan jaringan informal. Mereka yang sudah berada di dalam lingkaran kekuasaan memiliki keuntungan lebih besar untuk terus dipilih."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Mendambakan kepemimpinan perempuan dalam pemerintahan desa demi penguatan demokrasi","https://theconversation.com/mendambakan-kepemimpinan-perempuan-dalam-pemerintahan-desa-demi-penguatan-demokrasi-232292"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Jika setiap reshuffle hanya mengambil kandidat dari jaringan politik yang sama, pemerintah sebenarnya tidak sedang memperluas pilihan, melainkan hanya bermain di lingkaran kelompok semata."]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalan juga bukan sekadar apakah perempuan hadir, tetapi di mana mereka ditempatkan dan seberapa besar kewenangan yang mereka miliki."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Hasil kajian","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1468-0491.2007.00372.x"]," terhadap 72 negara menunjukkan bahwa keterwakilan perempuan dalam jabatan menteri berkaitan dengan faktor politik dan institusional. Kehadiran perempuan dalam posisi menteri juga dapat memperluas keterwakilan pada jenjang birokrasi di bawahnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karena itu, perempuan tidak seharusnya hanya ditempatkan pada sektor yang secara tradisional diasosiasikan dengan isu sosial, keluarga, pendidikan, atau kesejahteraan. Portofolio strategis seperti ekonomi, energi, teknologi, keamanan, diplomasi, dan politik juga harus terbuka bagi perempuan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Perempuan bukan pelengkap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pemerintah perlu berhenti melihat perempuan sebagai ",["pelengkap","https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-14781-4_1"]," untuk menampakkan citra kabinet yang inklusif."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Literatur politik","https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.4324/9781003572923-27/rethinking-public-sphere-contribution-critique-actually-existing-democracy-nancy-fraser"]," menunjukkan bahwa kehadiran perempuan dalam institusi politik dapat berpengaruh terhadap ",["perhatian pada kepentingan perempuan","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/j.1467-923X.2012.02265.x"],", meskipun hubungan antara jumlah perempuan dan perubahan kebijakan tidak selalu otomatis."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian","https://journal.unpad.ac.id/wacanapolitik/vol8/iss2/10/"]," tentang representasi perempuan juga masih banyak berfokus pada jumlah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Padahal, aspek keterwakilan yang bermakna membutuhkan perhatian lebih besar. Aspek ini terkait sejauh mana perempuan benar-benar memengaruhi kebijakan, dan sejauh mana perumusannya memperhitungkan kepentingan perempuan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pekerjaan rumah Indonesia dalam memerhatikan aspek ini masih banyak. Tengok saja kebijakan ",["perikanan","https://theconversation.com/perempuan-menjaga-rantai-dingin-demi-memastikan-ikan-sampai-ke-piring-tapi-kerjanya-kurang-diakui-291655"]," dan ",["pertanian","https://theconversation.com/perhutanan-sosial-masih-meminggirkan-perempuan-dalam-pengambilan-keputusan-berisiko-memperparah-ketimpangan-248444"]," yang masih mengabaikan peran perempuan di dalamnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Terjebak ‘Ibuisme’: mampukah Dharma Wanita menjadi organisasi progresif dalam perjuangan kesetaraan gender?","https://theconversation.com/terjebak-ibuisme-mampukah-dharma-wanita-menjadi-organisasi-progresif-dalam-perjuangan-kesetaraan-gender-216829"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Maka dari itu, ukuran keberhasilan pemerintah tidak seharusnya berhenti pada pertanyaan berapa banyak perempuan yang menjadi menteri atau anggota Wantimpres."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pertanyaan yang lebih penting adalah apakah mereka memiliki kesempatan yang sama untuk menentukan agenda, memengaruhi kebijakan, dan mengambil keputusan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jika pemerintah sungguh ingin membangun pemerintahan yang lebih efektif dan inklusif, solusinya bukan sekadar mencari lebih banyak perempuan untuk mengisi kursi kosong. Pemerintah perlu memperluas sumber rekrutmen—dari birokrasi, akademisi, profesional, masyarakat sipil, dunia usaha, hingga politik—agar tidak terus bergantung pada jaringan elite yang sama."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reshuffle yang hanya mengganti nama tanpa mengubah cara kekuasaan direkrut pada akhirnya bukan perubahan. Ia hanya reproduksi kekuasaan dengan wajah yang berbeda."]}],"chars":6202},"https://theconversation.com/true-crime-community-saat-internet-menjadi-tempat-anak-belajar-kekerasan-292986":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"87e388284daf8ca83e50116b549477f70e1ac1f048026b27262cfa832e86cdee","read":"https://theconversation.com/true-crime-community-saat-internet-menjadi-tempat-anak-belajar-kekerasan-292986","bytes":178673,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"True Crime Community: Saat internet menjadi tempat anak belajar kekerasan","by":[{"n":"Mochammad Wahyu Ghani","r":"Peneliti Pusat Riset Kependudukan, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"}],"pub":"2026-10-07T08:39:09Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Ruang digital dapat menormalisasi dan memperkuat perilaku kekerasan pada anak."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Kerentanan psikososial membuat anak lebih mudah terjebak komunitas kekerasan daring."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Pencegahan membutuhkan kolaborasi keluarga, sekolah, pemerintah, dan platform digital."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kasus kekerasan yang melibatkan anak dalam beberapa bulan terakhir menunjukkan pola yang semakin sulit diabaikan: ruang digital dapat menjadi tempat anak terpapar, mempelajari, bahkan menormalisasi kekerasan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada 7 Agustus 2026, seorang anak laki-laki berusia 14 tahun di ",["Nonthaburi, Thailand","https://www.bbc.com/indonesia/articles/c9w0x5xjd9go"],", menembak mati kakek dan neneknya di rumah. Ia kemudian pergi ke sekolah dan melepaskan tembakan ke arah guru dan siswa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sembilan orang tewas. ",["Investigasi","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cy07dern0n0o"]," kemudian menemukan bahwa anak tersebut mengikuti sejumlah komunitas daring yang membahas kekerasan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sebulan kemudian, pada 18 September 2026, seorang siswa berusia 16 tahun di ",["Cotabato Selatan, Filipina","https://kumparan.com/kumparannews/penembakan-di-sma-filipina-3-tewas-8-terluka-28Cv6KSa3zC"],", menembak teman-teman sekelasnya. Dua siswa tewas dan delapan lainnya terluka. Kasus ini juga dikaitkan dengan ",["True Crime Community (TCC)","https://www.ctvnews.ca/world/article/philippines-school-shooter-a-member-of-true-crime-community-best-friend-reportedly-told-officials/"],", yang sebelumnya turut disorot dalam penyelidikan penembakan di Tacloban pada Juni 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indonesia belum mengalami tragedi serupa dalam skala tersebut. Namun, risikonya bukan berarti tidak ada."]},{"k":"p","s":["Detasemen Khusus (Densus) 88 Antiteror Polri mengidentifikasi lebih dari ",["300 anak","https://regional.kompas.com/read/2026/09/17/090214078/densus-88-ungkap-lebih-dari-300-anak-terjebak-true-crime-community-rentan"]," yang terhubung dengan TCC melalui berbagai grup media sosial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anak-anak rentan karena ",["faktor psikososial","https://regional.kompas.com/read/2026/09/17/090214078/densus-88-ungkap-lebih-dari-300-anak-terjebak-true-crime-community-rentan"],", seperti keluarga yang tidak harmonis, minim perhatian orang tua, pengalaman perundungan, trauma psikologis, dan paparan konten kekerasan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Temuan ini penting karena persoalannya bukan sekadar apa yang ditonton anak di internet, tetapi apa yang terjadi ketika mereka terus-menerus terpapar, berinteraksi, dan mendapat penguatan dari komunitas tersebut."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Guru bukan manusia super menghadapi kekerasan di sekolah: Sekolah, pemerintah, dan masyarakat juga bertanggung jawab","https://theconversation.com/guru-bukan-manusia-super-menghadapi-kekerasan-di-sekolah-sekolah-pemerintah-dan-masyarakat-juga-bertanggung-jawab-287759"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Mengapa TCC berbahaya?"]},{"k":"p","s":[["TCC","https://ctc.westpoint.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/CTC-SENTINEL-022026_article-3.pdf"]," pada dasarnya adalah komunitas daring yang terbentuk dari ketertarikan terhadap kasus dan pelaku kejahatan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tidak semua orang yang menyukai konten true crime memiliki kecenderungan melakukan kekerasan. Risikonya muncul ketika ketertarikan terhadap kasus kriminal berkembang menjadi kekaguman terhadap pelaku atau normalisasi kekerasan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam teori ",["social learning","https://www.asecib.ase.ro/mps/Bandura_SocialLearningTheory.pdf"],", manusia dapat mempelajari perilaku dengan mengamati orang lain, terutama ketika perilaku tersebut terlihat mendatangkan perhatian, pengakuan, popularitas, atau penerimaan kelompok."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di ruang digital yang terbuka luas seperti saat ini, anak dapat melihat pelaku kekerasan terus-menerus dibicarakan, bahkan diperlakukan sebagai figur yang menarik atau terkenal. Bahkan dalam komunitas tertentu, tindakan ekstrem dapat memperoleh perhatian dan pengakuan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Peneliti Institute for Strategic Dialogue menyebut pola ini sebagai “ ",["memetic violence","https://www.isdglobal.org/digital-dispatch/how-the-true-crime-community-generates-its-own-killers/"],"”, yakni ketika pelaku baru mengambil unsur tertentu dari pelaku sebelumnya yang dikagumi, kemudian menirunya atau memodifikasinya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Risiko semakin besar ketika anak sedang mencari perhatian, identitas, atau rasa diterima yang tidak mereka dapatkan di rumah maupun sekolah. Komunitas daring kemudian dapat menjadi tempat mereka merasa memiliki kelompok."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Algoritma media sosial","https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/feb/06/social-media-algorithms-amplifying-misogynistic-content"]," yang kerap mempersempit lingkungan informasi membuat seseorang terus berinteraksi dengan konten serupa. Akhirnya, terbentuklah ",["echo chamber","https://www.aic.gov.au/sites/default/files/2023-06/ti673_understanding_and_preventing_internet-facilitated_radicalisation.pdf"]," (ruang gema), ketika satu pandangan terus diperkuat dan perspektif lain semakin jarang terlihat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tapi kita tetap perlu berhati-hati untuk tidak menyimpulkan bahwa TCC atau konten kekerasan adalah faktor tunggal yang membuat anak menjadi pelaku. Namun, ruang digital dapat menjadi salah satu lingkungan yang menyediakan pengetahuan, inspirasi, dan penguatan sosial bagi anak yang sudah berada dalam kondisi rentan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di Indonesia, sejumlah kasus kekerasan di lingkungan pendidikan juga menunjukkan bahwa anak telah menemukan cara membuat bahan peledak atau melakukan tindakan kekerasan melalui sumber-sumber di internet."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kasus di ",["SMAN 72 Jakarta Utara","https://www.kompas.id/artikel/teror-ledakan-di-sma-negeri-72-jakarta"],", ",["SMPN 3 Kalimantan Barat","https://www.bbc.com/indonesia/articles/c9wx949742qo"],", dan ",["MAN 3 Padang","https://www.bbc.com/indonesia/articles/cjrgrg301z3o"]," menunjukkan bahwa sekolah pun tidak terpisah dari risiko yang berkembang di ruang digital."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Dari tawuran ke ‘dark web’: Wajah baru kenakalan remaja","https://theconversation.com/dari-tawuran-ke-dark-web-wajah-baru-kenakalan-remaja-270974"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Anak tidak cukup hanya diawasi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Respons terhadap fenomena ini tidak bisa berhenti pada pemblokiran konten, razia gawai, atau penindakan hukum."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anak yang terpapar komunitas kekerasan perlu dilihat sebagai anak yang membutuhkan perlindungan sekaligus asesmen risiko, bukan semata-mata calon pelaku kriminal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sekolah perlu memiliki sistem deteksi perubahan perilaku, perundungan, isolasi sosial, dan ketertarikan yang semakin intens terhadap kekerasan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di rumah, orang tua juga perlu membangun komunikasi yang membuat anak merasa aman bercerita, bukan hanya memeriksa riwayat pencarian atau menyita telepon genggam."]},{"k":"p","s":["Densus 88 dan Badan Nasional Penanggulangan Teroris (BNPT) dapat berfokus pada identifikasi risiko kekerasan dan ekstremisme."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sedangkan Komisi Perlindungan Anak Indonesia (KPAI), Kementerian Pemberdayaan Perempuan dan Perlindungan Anak, dinas sosial, psikolog, dan layanan kesehatan jiwa memastikan anak mendapatkan pendampingan dan pemulihan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Platform digital juga perlu dimandatkan untuk bertanggung jawab membatasi distribusi konten yang mengglorifikasi pelaku kekerasan tanpa menghilangkan ruang diskusi publik yang sehat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fenomena ini bukan lagi persoalan satu-dua anak yang salah bergaul. Ini adalah risiko lintas sektor yang berada di persimpangan antara perlindungan anak, kesehatan mental, pendidikan, keamanan, dan teknologi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ruang digital tidak mungkin dikosongkan dari anak. Tapi jika terus diabaikan, ruang digital dapat berubah menjadi ruang belajar kekerasan yang bekerja diam-diam—dan anak-anak bisa menjadi murid sekaligus korbannya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Artikel ini berdasarkan kolaborasi bersama dengan Siska Azhari, peneliti ThinkTank.ID (Yayasan Pemikir Strategis Indonesia)."]}],"chars":5856},"https://theconversation.com/why-donald-trump-keeps-threatening-irans-pickaxe-mountain-and-why-it-is-so-hard-to-destroy-296071":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"7dccc618d0b0b0ca0c9642ee2922df2973e7f41ce3f6c35e3f06ca0931633320","read":"https://theconversation.com/why-donald-trump-keeps-threatening-irans-pickaxe-mountain-and-why-it-is-so-hard-to-destroy-296071","bytes":184942,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Why Donald Trump keeps threatening Iran’s Pickaxe Mountain – and why it is so hard to destroy","by":[{"n":"Arash Beidollahkhani","r":"Research Fellow at the Global Development Institute, University of Manchester"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T13:25:06Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Iran has become a test of Donald Trump’s credibility at home as well as his power abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["The war and ",["rising fuel prices","https://www.telegraph.co.uk/business/2026/11/04/stocks-dollar-midterm-elections-trump-ftse-100-markets/"]," contributed to the ",["Republican defeat","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqkgjvr00zmyo"]," in the recent congressional elections. That gives the president a stronger political reason to find an ending to ",["the conflict","https://theconversation.com/topics/us-iran-conflict-73960"]," that he can present as a success."]},{"k":"p","s":["On November 9, President Trump said he wanted to ",["keep the war at “status quo”","https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-us-trump-deal-negotiations/"],", but warned that American forces were “locked and loaded” should circumstances change."]},{"k":"p","s":["One mountain near Iran’s main nuclear complex sits at the centre of America’s conundrum. Trump ",["has","https://x.com/WhiteHouse/status/2082110891625996372"]," ",["repeatedly","https://www.newsweek.com/what-a-us-nuclear-strike-on-irans-pickaxe-mountain-could-look-like-12656972"]," threatened Pickaxe Mountain, ",["saying in October","https://www.reuters.com/world/trump-says-us-may-need-strike-irans-pickaxe-mountain-2026-10-16/"]," that the US could destroy it quickly. The gap between that promise and what a strike could achieve deserves attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickaxe Mountain is the English nickname for Kūh-e Kolang Gaz Lā, a 1,600m tall (5,200ft) peak located around 1 mile south of the Natanz nuclear complex in central Iran. Experts believe it hosts a nuclear facility, but it is thought to be much deeper than Natanz. According to experts, the ",["complex is located","https://apnews.com/article/iran-nuclear-natanz-uranium-enrichment-underground-project-04dae673fc937af04e62b65dd78db2e0"]," between 80m and 100m underground. This makes it more difficult to destroy than other sites associated with Tehran’s nuclear programme."]},{"k":"p","s":["The decision to build a complex at Pickaxe Mountain followed a series of explosions across Iran in 2020. These damaged alleged ",["missile sites","https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/29/world/middleeast/iran-missile-explosion.html"],", ",["power plants","https://www.timesofisrael.com/in-latest-in-series-of-blasts-in-iran-explosion-hits-power-plant-in-isfahan/"]," and other facilities. The causes remain unclear."]},{"k":"p","s":[["One blast","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-middle-east-53300579"],", on July 2, 2020, ",["damaged a workshop","https://isis-online.org/isis-reports/fire-and-explosion-in-the-new-natanz-centrifuge-assembly"]," at the Natanz nuclear complex that was used for assembling centrifuges. These centrifuges are containers used to produce enriched uranium. The uranium can be used for civilian nuclear power plants, but is also a component in nuclear weapons. In September of that year, the head of Iran’s Atomic Energy Organization said the workshop’s replacement ",["would be built","https://www.rferl.org/a/new-building-started-in-the-heart-of-the-mountain-near-iranian-uranium-facility/30827549.html"]," “in the heart” of Pickaxe Mountain."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The Trump administration’s concern","https://abcnews.com/Politics/pickaxe-mountain-trump-us-hit-iranian-nuclear-site/story?id=134957036"]," is that Pickaxe Mountain could shelter centrifuges capable of enriching uranium to weapons grade levels. ",["Analysts also suggest","https://www.csis.org/analysis/satellite-imagery-pickaxe-mountain"]," that the underground complex could accommodate other work related to developing a nuclear weapon."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Newspaper reports","https://www.timesofisrael.com/israeli-intel-said-to-show-iran-has-moved-centrifuges-to-natanzs-pickaxe-mountain/"]," citing Israeli intelligence assessments claim that Iran moved centrifuges and related equipment into its tunnels. The mountain could also provide ",["a protected base","https://factnameh.com/fa/fact-checks/2026-07-21-iran-pickaxe-mountain-natanz-nuclear-site"]," for rebuilding centrifuge production damaged in earlier attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["What is inside and how close it is to becoming operational remain publicly unverified. Satellite photographs show continued construction and reinforced entrances."]},{"k":"p","s":[["An assessment","https://www.csis.org/analysis/satellite-imagery-pickaxe-mountain"]," in September by the Centre for Strategic and International Studies (a thinktank based in the US) found an increased level of activity at Pickaxe Mountain during 2026. Analysts have not been able to confirm that centrifuges have been moved there, however."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Calls for nuclear weapons","https://monitoring.bbc.co.uk/product/b0006sk2"]," and a nuclear test in Iranian media and political circles, alongside speculation about Mojtaba Khamenei’s willingness to approve a shift towards nuclear deterrence, have added to concerns about the site."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the images alone cannot establish that enrichment or bomb making is happening inside. International inspectors have never been given access, leaving the interior’s layout and contents publicly unverified."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why is it difficult to attack?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The protection for the new facility comes from the mountain itself, which is composed ",["of dense granite","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/22/pickaxe-mountain-iran-nuclear-site-trump"],". The depth of 80-100m for the complex is an estimate drawn from external evidence; detailed plans have never been published."]},{"k":"p","s":["America’s largest conventional bunker-buster, ",["the GBU-57","https://www.twz.com/news-features/trumps-threat-to-strike-irans-pickaxe-mountain-bunkers-front-door-underscores-targeting-challenges"],", was used against Fordow and Natanz in June 2025. Its performance against Pickaxe Mountain remains uncertain. Figures describing penetration through earth tell us little about the same weapon’s performance through dense rock."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Trump administration could try to interrupt access and operations without reaching the deepest halls. ",["Public military assessments","https://www.newsweek.com/what-a-us-nuclear-strike-on-irans-pickaxe-mountain-could-look-like-12656972"]," discuss attacks on entrances and external infrastructure. Such damage could delay work, and repeated attacks could complicate repairs. Equipment buried deeper might survive."]},{"k":"p","s":["This creates a problem after the bombing stops. Satellite images can reveal a collapsed entrance. Establishing what happened far underground is much harder. A president could announce a successful operation while inspectors and analysts remain unable to verify its effect on Iran’s capabilities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Could a strike give Trump an exit?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickaxe Mountain offers Trump a target around which he could build a victory speech. After a politically costly war, a strike would let him claim that he had dealt with Iran’s remaining nuclear threat and could bring American operations to an end: damage the facility, ",["declare victory and withdraw","https://www.dw.com/en/can-us-midterm-election-really-change-trumps-iran-policy/a-79840683"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["That calculation is also being discussed inside Iran. One possible course would be to let Trump claim victory and avoid retaliation ",["so the war could end","https://www.politico.eu/article/skip-the-ted-talk-iran-mohammad-bagher-ghalibaf-trolls-us-jd-vance-over-midterm-defeat-analysis/"],". Claims that the Trump administration had requested such an arrangement ",["have circulated","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/08/us/politics/trump-iran-options.html"],". Iran’s foreign ministry, however, dismissed them and insisted that any attack would ",["receive a response","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-31/attacks-on-iran-should-be-met-without-restraint-khamenei-orders/107332392"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There could be an opportunity here for Tehran. If underground equipment survived and Trump accepted visible damage as grounds to leave, Iran could preserve capabilities while allowing the White House to claim success. The mountain could become a useful lure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet evidence that Iran has deliberately prepared such an outcome remains thin: construction began years before this confrontation. ",["Reinforcing the site","https://carnegieendowment.org/middle-east/diwan/2026/02/us-aims-with-iran-extend-beyond-the-nuclear-file"]," also serves the straightforward purpose of protecting it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even a spectacular strike would leave the ",["confrontation over shipping","https://www.iranintl.com/en/202611031361"]," through the Strait of Hormuz unresolved. The danger is that each side expects the other to stop. Trump could assume a limited attack would close the confrontation; Tehran could decide that answering it was essential to its credibility."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, damage visible from space would leave unanswered questions about equipment and material underground. Ending the confrontation would still require an agreement covering nuclear inspections, shipping through Hormuz, sanctions on Iran and the wider disputes keeping the conflict alive."]}],"chars":6104},"https://theconversation.com/la-relation-pekin-teheran-a-lepreuve-de-la-guerre-295808":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"993e6091df7a905488634a4189c114e209ced3e6501008c4bc47b2ca67dce933","read":"https://theconversation.com/la-relation-pekin-teheran-a-lepreuve-de-la-guerre-295808","bytes":193933,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"La relation Pékin-Téhéran à l’épreuve de la guerre","by":[{"n":"Thierry Kellner","r":"Chargé de cours (politique étrangère de la Chine), Université Libre de Bruxelles (ULB)"},{"n":"Mohammad Reza Djalili","r":"professeur émérite, Institut des hautes études internationales et de développement de Genève"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T16:10:23Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["L’ESSENTIEL"]},{"k":"li","s":["La guerre déclenchée par Israël et les États-Unis contre l’Iran met à l’épreuve le partenariat stratégique noué par ce dernier avec la Chine."]},{"k":"li","s":["Pékin soutient Téhéran par le pétrole, les équipements et la diplomatie, mais refuse de le défendre militairement."]},{"k":"li","s":["Dépendant de la Chine, l’Iran reste un atout géopolitique pour Pékin, qui entend l’aider sans partager sa guerre."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le 28 février 2026, les frappes américaines et israéliennes qui ont éliminé le guide suprême Ali Khamenei ont plongé l’Iran dans une guerre ouverte. Elles ont également mis à l’épreuve le « partenariat stratégique global » noué avec Pékin, ",["formalisé en 2021 par un accord de coopération de vingt-cinq ans","https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2021/03/27/teheran-et-pekin-signent-un-accord-de-cooperation-de-vingt-cinq-ans_6074669_3210.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Huit mois et demi plus tard, le constat est net : la Chine a aidé, protégé et outillé l’Iran, mais elle ne l’a jamais défendu, ce qui témoigne du ",["caractère limité de ce partenariat stratégique","https://www.inss.org.il/publication/china-iran-2026/"],". En réalité, cette limite n’a rien d’un accident. Elle procède d’un calcul chinois : pour Pékin, Téhéran compte peu dans sa balance économique, mais beaucoup sur l’échiquier géopolitique."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reste à comprendre jusqu’où va cette coopération, ce qui la borne et, au fond, lequel des deux partenaires sert l’autre."]},{"k":"h","s":["Une convergence d’intérêts réelle, mais inégale"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pour la Chine, l’Iran est d’abord un réservoir de brut à prix cassés. En 2025, elle en importait environ 1,4 million de barils par jour (Mb/j). Cela représentait 13 % de ses achats de brut et 80 à 90 % des exportations iraniennes. Ce pétrole, acheté avec un rabais d’environ 20 %, alimentait les raffineries indépendantes du Shandong (est de la Chine), surnommées ",["teapots refineries (« théières »), peu exposées au système financier américain","https://edition.cnn.com/2026/05/12/china/china-oil-refineries-iran-xi-trump-intl-hnk-dst"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Selon une lettre confidentielle du ministre iranien du pétrole par intérim ",["révélée par le média d’opposition basé à Londres Iran International","https://www.iranintl.com/en/202611090040"],", Téhéran contrôlerait, avec la « coopération discrète » de Pékin, des terminaux sur trois sites chinois et sept réservoirs de stockage. Il y gagne un accès direct aux raffineries, sans transbordement ni brut maquillé, et la possibilité de stocker son pétrole avant d’avoir trouvé un acheteur. La Chine, elle, y gagne des frais de stockage, un brut décoté livré à sa porte et, surtout, le bénéfice du démenti. Ses grandes banques et ses trois majors pétrolières restent à l’abri des sanctions, et Pékin garde la main : il refusait déjà avant la guerre de relever ses quotas et exigeait des rabais accrus. Quoi qu’il en soit, ce commerce est réglé en yuans par des intermédiaires hors de portée du Trésor américain, et le brut est souvent déclaré en partie comme « malaisien ». Ce mécanisme sert ainsi un dessein plus large : roder des circuits financiers affranchis du dollar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Vente par la Russie d’hydrocarbures à la Chine en yuan : fin du dollar, opportunité pour l’euro ?","https://theconversation.com/vente-par-la-russie-dhydrocarbures-a-la-chine-en-yuan-fin-du-dollar-opportunite-pour-leuro-265602"]]},{"k":"p","s":["L’intérêt chinois est aussi, et peut-être surtout, géopolitique. Les monarchies du Golfe abritent des bases américaines, et Israël est l’allié de Washington. Dans cette région, l’Iran est donc le seul État de poids qui échappe à l’orbite sécuritaire des États-Unis. Il retient en outre l’attention et les moyens militaires américains loin de l’Indo-Pacifique. L’avantage est d’autant plus précieux que ce partenariat ne coûte presque rien à Pékin."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pour Téhéran, la Chine est une bouée de sauvetage irremplaçable. Au plus fort des combats, en mars, les raffineries « teapots » ont importé un ",["record de 1,8 Mb/j","https://www.bairdmaritime.com/amp/story/shipping/tankers/china-burns-through-crude-stockpiles-after-massive-import-drop."],". En avril, Pékin a, avec Moscou, opposé, son ",["veto","https://news.un.org/fr/story/2026/04/1158658"]," à un projet de résolution exigeant la réouverture du détroit d’Ormuz. Surtout, des entreprises chinoises ont fourni ce que l’État chinois ne pouvait assumer ouvertement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Selon le ",["Wall Street Journal","https://www.wsj.com/politics/china-iran-aid-xi-trump-summit-e6541ae8?eafs_enabled=false"],", quelque 1 300 envois de composants à double usage, utiles aux drones et au guidage des missiles, ont été expédiés au premier semestre 2026. Le ",["Financial Times","https://www.ft.com/content/1fddd2cd-1294-4e9c-a17d-5ea06b399355"]," affirme aussi que les Gardiens de la révolution ont acquis un satellite d’observation chinois, le TEE-01B, pour photographier des bases américaines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pékin ",["dément","https://www.uscc.gov/research/enabling-iran-timeline-chinas-role-during-and-after-operation-epic-fury"],". On peut y voir une logique de « déni plausible » : il s’agirait d’ ",["aider sans s’exposer","https://www.grip.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-07-RA-TK-NL-Chine-guerre-Iran-Irael.pdf"],". En retour, Téhéran promet aux navires chinois des « considérations spéciales » sur les frais de passage qu’il entend imposer à Ormuz."]},{"k":"h","s":["Les bornes du soutien : ni alliance ni sacrifice"]},{"k":"p","s":["La première borne est militaire. Pékin n’a engagé ni soldat ni navire. Le 11 mars, il s’est abstenu sur la ",["résolution 2817 du Conseil de sécurité","https://cdi.ulb.ac.be/ladoption-par-le-conseil-de-securite-de-la-resolution-2817-2026-quelles-consequences-sur-linterpretation-du-droit-de-legitime-defense/"],", qui condamnait les frappes iraniennes contre les monarchies du Golfe."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cette neutralité affichée n’avait rien de neutre, puisqu’elle émoussait la portée du texte. L’activisme chinois a pris la forme d’une « médiation sans engagement ». Le 31 mars, Pékin a présenté avec le Pakistan un ",["plan de paix en cinq points","https://www.rfi.fr/fr/moyen-orient/20260331-guerre-au-moyen-orient-la-chine-et-le-pakistan-pr%C3%A9sentent-un-plan-en-cinq-points-pour-une-r%C3%A9solution-du-conflit"],". Le ministre des affaires étrangères Wang Yi a multiplié les entretiens avec ses homologues, plus d’une trentaine. La Chine a aussi soutenu sans relâche le ",["mémorandum d’Islamabad","https://spa.gov.sa/fr/N2615384"]," signé le 17 juin 2026 par Donald Trump et son homologue iranien Massoud Pezeshkian, sous la médiation du Pakistan (avec l’appui de l’Arabie saoudite, du Qatar, de la Turquie et de l’Égypte). Donald Trump a également ",["assuré","https://www.bfmtv.com/international/amerique-nord/etats-unis/donald-trump/donald-trump-assure-que-xi-jinping-n-enverra-pas-d-equipement-militaire-a-l-iran-et-qu-il-a-propose-son-aide-pour-rouvrir-le-detroit-d-ormuz_AD-202605140561.html"]," que, en mai, Xi Jinping lui a promis de ne pas vendre d’armes à l’Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cette retenue tient aussi à l’état de l’outil militaire. Elle n’est pas nouvelle : hors de ",["sa base de Djibouti","https://www.rfi.fr/fr/afrique/20260919-%C3%A0-djibouti-p%C3%A9kin-renforce-les-capacit%C3%A9s-de-surveillance-r%C3%A9gionale-de-sa-base-militaire"],", la Chine ne s’est jamais dotée jusqu’ici des moyens de projeter durablement sa puissance au Moyen-Orient. Mais la purge sans précédent que Xi Jinping mène dans l’Armée populaire de libération (APL) la renforce. Selon la ",["base de données du CSIS","https://www.csis.org/analysis/assessing-xis-unprecedented-purges-chinas-military-key-developments-and-potential"],", 101 des quelque 176 plus hauts responsables militaires, soit 52 %, ont été limogés ou ont disparu depuis 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["En janvier 2026, le premier vice-président de la Commission militaire centrale, Zhang Youxia, et le chef d’état-major interarmées, Liu Zhenli, ont été écartés. Ils ont été exclus du Parti en septembre pour « déloyauté ». Tous deux comptaient parmi les derniers généraux ayant connu le feu (contre le Vietnam, lors de la guerre de 1979 et des affrontements frontaliers des années 1980). La Commission comptait sept membres en 2022 ; elle n’en conserve que deux en activité – Xi lui-même et le général Zhang Shengmin, chargé de la discipline et qui vient d’être promu au Politburo du Parti communiste chinois (PCC). Une première depuis trente-deux ans ! Même Zhong Shaojun, longtemps l’homme de confiance de Xi, a été évincé."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les effets sont mesurables. En 2025, l’APL a mis 19 puis 12 jours à organiser ses grandes manœuvres autour de Taïwan, contre 4 jours en 2024. Le théâtre Est, chargé de Taïwan, est resté neuf mois sans commandant. Taylor Fravel décrit une ",["direction « organisationnellement décapitée »","https://csis-website-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/s3fs-public/2026-02/260224_Lin_Xi_Purges.pdf"],", dont la capacité à conduire une opération d’ampleur est désormais douteuse. Ces purges ne signalent pas pour autant un pouvoir affaibli. Elles traduisent au contraire une personnalisation croissante, où la loyauté envers Xi prime sur la compétence et où l’armée perd l’autonomie professionnelle que le Parti lui concédait jusque-là."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ce type de pouvoir a son revers : des ",["officiers qui n’osent plus dire au chef ce qui ne fonctionne pas","https://inss.ndu.edu/Media/News/Article/4541489/pla-autonomy-and-the-chinese-military-purges/"],". Pour l’Iran, la conclusion est sans appel. Une armée en reconstruction, absorbée par l’objectif taïwanais et par l’impératif de loyauté, n’a ni les moyens ni la vocation de s’aventurer dans le Golfe. Les purges ne créent pas la retenue chinoise : elles la verrouillent."]},{"k":"p","s":["La deuxième borne est le golfe Persique, où se jouent les intérêts économiques réels de la Chine. En 2025, celle-ci a ",["échangé","https://www.inss.org.il/publication/china-middle-east-2026/"]," environ 108 milliards de dollars de biens avec l’Arabie saoudite, et autant avec les Émirats arabes unis. Avec l’Iran, ce commerce n’atteint qu’une dizaine de milliards, pétrole non compris : l’Irak, à lui seul, pèse cinq fois plus."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’écart est plus grand encore pour les investissements. De 2005 à 2025, la Chine a investi environ 4,7 milliards de dollars en Iran, contre 15,6 milliards en Israël et près de 45 milliards dans les monarchies du Golfe. Les 400 milliards souvent associés à l’accord de 2021 n’apparaissent dans aucun texte connu. Seuls ",["185 millions auraient été investis à ce titre","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/iranian-studies/article/between-new-axis-of-evil-and-paper-tiger-expectations-and-reality-of-the-25year-iran-china-cooperation-agreement/660DD73AA254337D12D2D8B8E83F466A"],". En frappant Riyad et Abou Dhabi, Téhéran a donc touché les deux premiers partenaires de Pékin dans la région. Le message n’a pas échappé à Xi Jinping. Après le cessez-le-feu d’avril, il a reçu le prince héritier d’Abou Dhabi et appelé Mohammed ben Salmane, sans avoir de geste comparable envers Téhéran."]},{"k":"p","s":["La troisième borne sont les États-Unis. Les deux sommets entre Xi et Trump, ",["à Pékin en mai","https://www.ifri.org/fr/presse-contenus-repris-sur-le-site/sommet-donald-trump-xi-jinping-la-treve-entre-la-chine-et-les"]," puis ",["à Washington en septembre","https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/09/25/donald-trump-accueille-xi-jinping-en-majeste-a-la-maison-blanche-pour-celebrer-la-stabilite-strategique-entre-les-etats-unis-et-la-chine_6781787_3210.html"],", ont montré que la stabilisation de la relation sino-américaine prime sur le sort de Téhéran."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les sanctions secondaires américaines, qui visent les entreprises étrangères commerçant avec l’Iran, ont frappé la raffinerie chinoise Hengli Petrochemical (Dalian) Refinery Co. en avril, puis ",["trois entreprises chinoises d’imagerie satellitaire en mai","https://fr.finance.yahoo.com/actualites/%C3%A9tats-unis-sanctionnent-entreprises-chinoises-070710304.html"],". L’opération ",["« Economic Outcast »","https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0643"]," a visé une soixantaine de cibles en août, dont des entreprises chinoises basées à Hongkong, Qingdao et Shenzhen. Washington a toutefois épargné les grandes banques chinoises : l’escalade a ses bornes, des deux côtés."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le blocus naval américain, rétabli à la mi-juillet, a achevé de tarir le flux. Les importations chinoises de brut iranien sont tombées à environ 0,5 Mb/j en septembre. Aucune cargaison n’a été chargée en Iran ce mois-là, et le pétrole iranien stocké en mer hors d’Ormuz était épuisé à la mi-octobre."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pékin, lui, a déjà trouvé d’autres fournisseurs. Ses importations depuis le Golfe, tombées à 3,5 Mb/j en septembre, devraient dépasser 5 Mb/j en octobre, presque le niveau d’avant-guerre (5,6 Mb/j). Riyad et Bagdad ont baissé leurs prix pour reconquérir le client chinois, et les ",["achats de brut russe dépassent de 20 % leur niveau d’il y a un an","https://www.iranintl.com/en/202610222999"],". Le pétrole iranien est devenu remplaçable."]},{"k":"h","s":["Nommer la relation : qui sert qui ?"]},{"k":"p","s":["La Chine ",["n’a pas de politique iranienne en soi","https://arabcenterdc.org/resource/what-the-iran-war-reveals-about-chinas-middle-east-strategy/"],". Elle lit chaque crise régionale à l’aune de sa rivalité avec Washington, en y cherchant à la fois un levier et une mise à l’abri. Côté iranien, la déception n’a pas tourné au ressentiment. Les experts iraniens ",["reprochent moins à Pékin sa tiédeur qu’à Téhéran de n’avoir jamais défini ce qu’il attendait de la Chine","https://chinamed.it/observer/from-look-east-to-learn-china-irans-expert-debate-on-china-and-the-ceasefire"],". Le réformiste Kioomars Ashtarian résume le malentendu : la Chine s’est conduite en médiatrice, non en alliée. D’autres redoutent un « grand marchandage » sino-américain conclu aux dépens de l’Iran. Le consensus n’en est pas moins net : pour Hamed Vafaei, travailler avec Pékin n’est plus « un choix, mais une nécessité », ce dont témoigne la ",["nomination","https://www.tasnimnews.ir/en/news/2026/05/17/3592987/qalibaf-assigned-as-iran-s-special-representative-for-china-affairs"],", en mai, du président du Parlement, Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf, au poste de représentant spécial pour la Chine (une nomination qui reflète aussi l’emprise croissante de l’appareil sécuritaire sur la politique chinoise de Téhéran)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Plusieurs concepts permettent de qualifier ce lien. Le ",["« partenariat stratégique global »","https://academic.oup.com/cjip/article/10/1/31/2958616"]," relève d’une diplomatie chinoise des partenariats hiérarchisés, qui confère un statut sans créer d’obligation. Il s’agit d’un ",["alignement","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/review-of-international-studies/article/abs/alignment-not-alliance-the-shifting-paradigm-of-international-security-cooperation-toward-a-conceptual-taxonomy-of-alignment/0C7B86297FC2A61539D1944DF60AC405"]," plutôt que d’une alliance. ",["Glenn Snyder","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/world-politics/article/abs/security-dilemma-in-alliance-politics/681B1AF11D96E61995028026205CE783"]," distinguait deux peurs au sein des alliances : être abandonné par son allié, ou être entraîné par lui dans une guerre qui n’est pas la sienne, ce qu’il appelait le « piégeage ». C’est la seconde qui domine à Pékin. Cela relativise la ",["thèse d’un « axe des perturbateurs »","https://www.foreignaffairs.com/china/axis-upheaval-russia-iran-north-korea-taylor-fontaine"]," soudé autour de la Chine, de la Russie, de l’Iran et de la Corée du Nord."]},{"k":"p","s":["La lecture triangulaire, inspirée de ",["Lowell Dittmer","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/world-politics/article/abs/strategic-triangle-an-elementary-gametheoretical-analysis/F0C8847A042646DB8FA9B8D8C8BB37A1"],", éclaire le reste. Pékin attribue à chacun de ses partenaires une fonction distincte plutôt que de les équilibrer : il demande la technologie à Israël et l’énergie à l’Iran. La guerre a fait de cette « triangulation d’opportunité » une triangulation sous contrainte."]},{"k":"p","s":["La relation relève enfin de ",["l’interdépendance asymétrique","https://www.ucpress.edu/books/national-power-and-the-structure-of-foreign-trade/paper"],": celui qui dépend le moins de l’autre détient le pouvoir. Dans le vocabulaire des ",["études sur les sanctions","https://e-edu.nbu.bg/pluginfile.php/139618/mod_resource/content/0/pol-222KeohaneNye-Interdepend.pdf"],", la Chine tient le rôle du ",["« chevalier noir »","https://www.sup.org/books/politics/busted-sanctions"],", qui permet à un régime sanctionné de survivre. Elle le fait toutefois par des canaux commerciaux « privés », qui lui laissent le bénéfice de pouvoir démentir."]},{"k":"p","s":["Qui sert qui, alors ? Sur le plan économique, la réponse ne fait guère de doute : la Chine est bien plus utile à l’Iran que l’inverse. Elle absorbait l’essentiel du pétrole iranien, qui ne pesait qu’un huitième de ses propres importations. La guerre a encore creusé l’écart. Adossé à une réserve stratégique estimée à 1,3 milliard de barils, Pékin avait gonflé ses stocks dès janvier. Téhéran, lui, voit fondre sa dernière rente, et la Chine pourra ",["monnayer cette détresse en rabais","https://foreignpolicy.com/2026/06/16/china-iran-war-lessons-energy-oil-diplomacy/"],", comme elle l’a fait avec la Russie après 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sur l’échiquier géopolitique, en revanche, l’Iran reste irremplaçable. Il occupe Washington loin de l’Asie de l’Est et peut servir de monnaie d’échange face à Donald Trump. Il fournit aussi un terrain d’essai à une finance hors dollar et un poste d’observation sur l’usure des arsenaux américains."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pékin s’emploie déjà à tisser des liens avec les Gardiens de la révolution, devenus le ",["nouveau centre de gravité du pouvoir iranien","https://theconversation.com/iran-du-regime-des-mollahs-au-regime-des-gardiens-278388"],". Ashtarian conseille d’ailleurs à Téhéran de faire valoir sa capacité de nuisance à Ormuz pour se rendre indispensable. C’est reconnaître que le seul levier de l’Iran sur la Chine est négatif."]},{"k":"h","s":["Un partenaire nécessaire, un allié introuvable"]},{"k":"p","s":["L’asymétrie qui borne la relation est aussi ce qui la rend durable. Téhéran n’a pas d’autre client, et Pékin, s’il trouve d’autres fournisseurs de pétrole, n’a aucun équivalent régional à l’Iran dans la zone. La Chine continuera donc de soutenir le régime iranien juste assez pour qu’il survive, mais jamais assez pour être entraînée dans sa guerre."]},{"k":"p","s":["Trois variables décideront à court terme de cet équilibre. La première est la possibilité d’une ",["reprise des frappes américaines après les élections de mi-mandat du 3 novembre dernier","https://www.ouest-france.fr/monde/etats-unis/donald-trump/le-president-americain-donald-trump-juge-tres-improbable-une-reprise-de-la-guerre-en-iran-36e5a850-dc11-11f1-a45f-49114163a350"],". La deuxième est l’extension possible des sanctions aux grandes banques chinoises. La troisième est le rôle que Pékin entend jouer dans une reconstruction iranienne qu’il imagine déjà. Le plus probable des scénarios est celui d’une « triangulation adaptative » qui recalibrerait ce jeu sans le bouleverser. Seul un effondrement du régime iranien en déferait la logique."]}],"chars":14168},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cambodia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-20T17:04Z","sha":"daa9e6f7dae39bea5c13c97ab7ab2645af6322a6e5697c0939b245f2c3d8c5c9","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/cambodia","bytes":72236,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Cambodia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-05T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-18T15:21:31+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to within 20km from the land border with Thailand."]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy fighting along parts of the Thailand and Cambodia border, including the use of airstrikes, rocket and artillery fire, took place in 2025. A ceasefire was signed on 27 December, but the situation remains tense."]},{"k":"p","s":["Land borders and crossings between Cambodia and Thailand continue to be suspended. Some tourist destinations in border areas such as the Preah Vihear/Khao Phra Wihan temple, the Ta Krabey/Ta Kwai temple and the Tamone Thom/Ta Muen Thom temple are closed."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are also unexploded ordnance, including landmines, in the border area."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cambodia/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Cannabis and drug offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to carry cannabis out of Cambodia. British nationals have been arrested for attempting to take cannabis out of the country, including while transiting through other countries. Many international airports use advanced screening technology and may scan the baggage of transit passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drug offences, including the possession, use and trafficking of cannabis, are serious crimes in Cambodia. If you are found carrying cannabis or other illegal drugs, you can be arrested and may face a lengthy prison sentence of up to 30 years. Do not carry bags, packages or items for other people. You are responsible for anything found in your luggage."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more information about illegal drugs on the ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cambodia/safety-and-security"]," page."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cambodia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Cambodia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Cambodia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Royal Embassy of Cambodia in the UK","https://www.cambodiaembassyuk.org/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Cambodia your passport must be:"]},{"k":"li","s":["valid for at least 6 months from the date you arrive in Cambodia"]},{"k":"li","s":["undamaged and complete – entry is normally refused if you have a damaged passport or pages missing"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you apply to renew or extend your visa from within Cambodia, your passport must be valid for at least 6 months from the start date of that subsequent renewal or extension."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Cambodia as a visitor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourist visas are valid for 30 days from the date of entry into Cambodia. Make sure your passport is stamped on arrival and keep the departure form. If you lose your departure form, you’ll need to contact immigration officials before you leave the country to make alternative arrangements."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a tourist visa"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Apply for an e-visa","https://www.cambodiaembassyuk.org/visa-cosular-services/apply-e-visa/"]," at least 4 days in advance (this website may not work in certain web browsers). You can also apply on the official e-visa app on ",["iOS","https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/evisa-cambodia/id1436702505"]," or ",["Android","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.ptel.cambodia_evisa&hl=en-US"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with the ",["Royal Embassy of Cambodia in the UK","https://www.cambodiaembassyuk.org/"]," for the latest information on fees, conditions and photograph requirements. If you do not get an e-visa, you can get a visa on arrival at airports or land border crossings. You need to provide a photo and pay in US dollars."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also get an extension of a tourist visa while you are in Cambodia."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can be fined, detained and deported if you overstay your visa. There is no limit to this fine. If you overstay more than 30 days, you will need to leave Cambodia and pay the fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Electronic arrival card"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 1 September 2024, Cambodia implemented an electronic Arrival Card. If you are entering Cambodia by air at either Phnom Penh, Siem Reap or Sihanoukville international airports, you must complete and submit an electronic ",["e-Arrival Card","https://arrival.gov.kh/"]," within 7 days prior to your arrival. There is no charge for this."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Business visas and work permits"]},{"k":"p","s":["Business visas are issued by the immigration department and are available:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on arrival in Phnom Penh airport"]},{"k":"li","s":["at the immigration department"]},{"k":"li","s":["in advance from any Cambodian embassy"]},{"k":"p","s":["To work in Cambodia you need a business visa and a work permit. Your employer will need to apply for your work permit from the Department of Labour and Social Affairs."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Cambodian government strictly enforces these rules, so ask the relevant department for the latest advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Cambodia, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Cambodia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/39/cambodia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Cambodian Department of Immigration runs an online registration app called the ",["Foreigners Present in Cambodia System (FPCS)","https://fpcs.immigration.gov.kh/login"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying in a hotel, guesthouse or rented accommodation, make sure the manager or landlord registers you using the app."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are staying with friends or family or own your own home in Cambodia, you will need to register yourself, using the app for ",["Android","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=fpcs.immigration.gov.kh&hl=en"]," or ",["iOS","https://apps.apple.com/us/app/fpcs-gdi/id1484912224"],". You need to enter a Cambodian phone number for your registration to be valid."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you fail to get yourself registered, you may be unable to extend your visa if you want to."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Cambodia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Cambodia, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by expatriates and foreign travellers. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Land borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert to the local security situation in border regions and at land crossings between countries. Get local advice before you set off. At the more remote crossing points, conditions can be basic. Local officials and tour operators can ask for unofficial fees or inflate visa prices at land borders. Make sure you know the correct visa requirements and fees before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid all protests, demonstrations and student and political rallies as they can become violent without warning."]},{"k":"h","s":["Landmines"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cambodia remains heavily affected by landmines and unexploded weapons. Mined areas are often unmarked. Do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stray off main routes in rural areas, including around temple complexes"]},{"k":"li","s":["pick up metal objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Organised crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["A bomb was left near a casino in Phnom Penh in December 2022 and there was a shooting in the same month. Both were likely linked to organised crime, and tourists were not targeted."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most incidents of theft are bag snatchings, often by thieves riding past on motorbikes. Thieves will cut bag straps and snatch bags or phones from tourists on foot or in tuk-tuks and on motorbikes, often causing injury. There have been incidents on bus journeys where passengers have had items taken from bags while asleep."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hotspots for petty crime include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the riverfront and BKK areas of Phnom Penh"]},{"k":"li","s":["the beaches and tourist areas of Sihanoukville and nearby islands"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your risk from street crime:"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a hotel safe for your valuables"]},{"k":"li","s":["take extra care at night and in isolated areas and stick to well-used, well-lit roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry a personal alarm if possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["minimise the items you carry with you"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry bags on the side of you that is furthest from the road"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not place bags in the front basket of bicycles"]},{"k":"li","s":["try to travel in tuk-tuks with metal grills on the back and side that offer some protection against bag snatching"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Female travellers, including British nationals, have been sexually assaulted in Siem Reap and Sihanoukville. This includes incidents of lone women being sexually assaulted by men claiming to be motorbike taxi drivers in the Pub Street area of Siem Reap. Be wary of approaches from strangers and offers of transport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Parties, including organised dance parties on Cambodia’s islands, may place you at risk of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["sexual assault"]},{"k":"li","s":["robbery"]},{"k":"li","s":["injury"]},{"k":"li","s":["arrest"]},{"k":"li","s":["losing belongings, including travel documents"]},{"k":"p","s":["Islands are often isolated and access to medical or emergency assistance is limited or non-existent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cambodians are friendly, but you should be wary if a Cambodian or other foreign national befriends you quickly and invites you to their home or hotel to meet their family."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police have reported instances of drink spiking in some bars visited by foreign nationals. Do not leave drinks unattended."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in Cambodia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers have reported fake dollar bills being given as change in shops and clubs. Check that notes you receive are genuine and are not damaged or torn."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be sceptical if offered an opportunity of easy work. Organised crime groups operate sophisticated job scams, advertising ‘easy jobs with high pay’. They traffic victims – some of them from neighbouring countries – mostly to secure compounds in and around Sihanoukville, border areas and Kandal. These jobs have turned out to be long hours of factory work where pay was low, passports withheld and free movement was allegedly restricted."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["It may be useful to carry a copy of the photo page of your passport, but this is not a legal requirement in Cambodia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Legal system and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal process in Cambodia is unpredictable, lacks transparency and is open to interference from political and business interests. The investigation and trial process falls far below the standard of the UK. Pre-trial detention can also last many months. The British Embassy will not interfere in the legal processes of a host country."]},{"k":"p","s":["The conditions in Cambodian prisons are extremely poor and overcrowded. Medical facilities in prisons are also very poor. The UK has no prisoner transfer agreement with Cambodia so if you’re found guilty you can expect to serve your full prison term in Cambodia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession, trafficking and manufacture of any illegal drugs are serious offences in Cambodia. This includes cannabis. British nationals have been caught carrying cannabis while transiting through Cambodia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Cambodia have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Cambodia authorities have a zero-tolerance policy to drug offences. Possessing drugs, even in very small quantities, can carry severe penalties, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["arrest and detention"]},{"k":"li","s":["a long jail sentence if charged and convicted. This can include a life sentence with no reduction for good behaviour"]},{"k":"p","s":["Legal processes before court hearings can be long and expensive. It can take many months for a case to come to trial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminal gangs in the UK and elsewhere have been known to coerce people into carrying drugs across borders. Do not allow yourself to be persuaded."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is important to be aware of your rights if you are detained by the police. See ",["our guidance for those detained or imprisoned in Cambodia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cambodia-prisoner-pack"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Police often raid venues known to be frequented by foreigners. You may have to take a urine or blood test if there is a suspicion you have used drugs. You will be arrested if the test is positive."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Angkor Wat official code of conduct"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Cambodian authorities have issued an ",["official code of conduct for visitors","https://www.siemreap.net/guides/angkor/angkor-visitor-code-of-conduct/"]," at Angkor Wat and other religious sites."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be refused admission to religious sites, including Angkor Wat, if you wear skirts or shorts above the knee. Cover bare shoulders."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Never take photographs on or near military bases. Ask permission before taking pictures of people, especially monks and other religious figures."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Research, photography and filming"]},{"k":"p","s":["Request permission in advance from the district head, provincial governor or national tourism board for any travel that authorities might see as out of the ordinary, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["scientific research of any kind"]},{"k":"li","s":["carrying out surveys"]},{"k":"li","s":["extensive photography or filming"]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Cambodia. The LGBT+ community is becoming more visible, through gay clubs, club nights and the work of some human rights organisations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Adopting Cambodian children"]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK government has ",["suspended all adoptions of Cambodian children by UK residents","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/intercountry-adoption-list-of-restricted-countries"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Commercial surrogacy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Commercial surrogacy is banned in Cambodia. If you pay a surrogate, you could get a fine or a prison sentence. See ",["guidance on surrogacy abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/surrogacy-overseas"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Phone and data connections"]},{"k":"p","s":["While there is good wi-fi and mobile phone networks in the main cities and towns of Cambodia, many of the islands and remote areas are not well covered. Make sure your friends and family are aware that you may be out of contact."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health and safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cambodia does not have the same health and safety standards as in the UK. Be aware that safety advice will be minimal and there may be no warning signs about dangers at tourist sites."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Jungle treks"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re considering jungle trekking, use a reputable tour guide. There’s no licensing system for tour guides, so get advice from your hotel, and look at online reviews before hiring a guide."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water-based activities"]},{"k":"p","s":["When swimming, kayaking, rafting, or using jet-skis:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take extra care in the rainy season from May to October"]},{"k":"li","s":["watch for river currents – these can be extremely strong and there have been fatalities because of this"]},{"k":"li","s":["beware of jellyfish in the sea close to the shore – their sting can be fatal"]},{"k":"li","s":["take local advice from hotel management and rent equipment only from recommended operators"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for damage before using any equipment"]},{"k":"li","s":["insist on training and ask operators to explain safe practices"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ⁠ ",["watersports safety advice","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"]," from the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents (ROSPA)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Diving school standards are not always as high as in the UK. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check a dive operator’s credentials"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you’re covered by insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure safety equipment is available on the boat, particularly oxygen"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask about safety precautions, including the ability to transfer divers to a hyperbaric chamber"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have not had any previous diving experience:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask your dive instructor to explain what cover they offer before signing up"]},{"k":"li","s":["check what to do if something goes wrong, including how to call for help while at sea"]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Cambodia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". Cambodia has one of the highest rates of road traffic accidents in south-east Asia. There are large numbers of fatalities and serious injuries. Many accidents are due to poor vehicle and driver safety standards. Travel after dark significantly increases the risk of accidents."]},{"k":"p","s":["To hire a car or a motorcycle over 125cc, you may sometimes need to have the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you hire any vehicle, check drivers and any passengers are covered by your travel insurance and check the small print of the rental agreement."]},{"k":"p","s":["For long-term car rental or to drive a private car, you need to get a Cambodian driving licence. Local travel agencies or car hire firms can help arrange this for a fee. Bring an IDP and your UK licence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Motorcycles"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travelling as a passenger by motorcycle taxi (‘moto dop’) is dangerous. Vehicles are poorly maintained and driving standards are low. There is also a risk that thieves (also on motorcycles) will snatch bags from off your bike, particularly in Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville."]},{"k":"p","s":["The police can impose an on-the-spot fine if you ride a motorcycle without a helmet. Riding without a helmet may also invalidate your insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not hand over your passport as a guarantee for returning a motorcycle or scooter."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea and river travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Accidents have happened when boats are overloaded or poorly maintained. Tourist boats sometimes operate despite weather warnings, particularly between Sihanoukville and the nearby islands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Water levels in rivers and lakes are high during the rainy season from June to October, making currents faster and more dangerous. Boat travel on rivers is difficult in the dry season, from March to May, due to the exposure of sandbars and other hazards that can damage boats or cause them to run aground."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Mekong River Commission","https://www.mrcmekong.org/"]," posts official updates on the Mekong River."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Monsoon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy storms during the monsoon season from June to October disrupt and damage the road network. Travel to some provinces can be seriously restricted by landslides at this time. Poor drainage results in flooded roads, causing major traffic congestion and delays in Phnom Penh - including along the route to the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local news and weather reports, and ",["weather updates from the World Meteorological Organisation","https://worldweather.wmo.int/en/country.html?countryCode=KHM"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lakes, caves and waterfalls are particularly prone to dangerous flash flooding during the rainy season from June to October."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 119 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Cambodia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/39/cambodia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Cambodia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/39/cambodia"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["Schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"li","s":["biting insects and ticks"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Cambodia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Cambodia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cambodia-list-of-medical-and-dental-services--2"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-cambodia#healthcare-and-medication"]," if you’re living in Cambodia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Cambodia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 117"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 118"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 119"]},{"k":"h","s":["Tourist police in Cambodia"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to report a crime, you can go to the tourist police."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get a police report for insurance purposes, but police are not always willing to investigate crimes."]},{"k":"p","s":["A police report should be free. If police ask for a fee ",["contact the British Embassy in Phnom Penh","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/cambodia/british-embassy-phnom-penh"]," and give details of the police station."]},{"k":"p","s":["To report a crime:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Phnom Penh, go to the Tourist Police at Street 598, 12107 (Tel +855 (0)12 942 484)"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Siem Reap, go to the Tourist Police office which is next to the ticketing booth for the Angkor temple ruins"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Sihanoukville, Battambang and other towns in Cambodia, check with the local police which police station you should report to"]},{"k":"p","s":["Local law enforcement response to a crime, including a violent crime, is often limited. Foreigners attempting to report crimes have found:"]},{"k":"li","s":["police stations closed"]},{"k":"li","s":["emergency telephone numbers unanswered"]},{"k":"li","s":["police unwilling to investigate"]},{"k":"li","s":["police unable to speak English"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Cambodia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=cambodia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?country=Cambodia&serviceType=translatorsInterpreters"]," in Cambodia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Cambodia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cambodia-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Cambodia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cambodia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/cambodia/british-embassy-phnom-penh"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/cambodia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Cambodia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-cambodia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":23682,"change":"New information about cannabis and drug offences (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/netherlands":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"507c273a6b9e083c626b06cce7b78d14070fedf378fd469644266c2b9dec41b3","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/netherlands","bytes":81982,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Netherlands travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-24T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:20:34+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["separate travel advice pages","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," for advice on travel to the constituent countries and special municipalities in the Dutch Caribbean."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/netherlands/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the Netherlands’ current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in the Netherlands set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Netherlands Embassy in the UK","https://www.netherlandsworldwide.nl/contact/embassies-consulates-general/united-kingdom/embassy-london"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Netherlands follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel without a visa to the Schengen area, which includes the Netherlands, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["or for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in the Netherlands","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-the-netherlands-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day limit. Visits to Schengen countries within the previous 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in the Netherlands","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-the-netherlands#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the Dutch government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need on the ",["Dutch government website","https://www.government.nl/topics/immigration-to-the-netherlands/question-and-answer/which-visa-do-i-need-to-travel-to-the-netherlands"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in the Netherlands with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Temporary border controls"]},{"k":"p","s":["Netherlands has introduced additional entry checks until 8 June 2026. Checks may be carried out on major roads leading into Netherlands, international trains and on intra-Schengen flights. See information from ",["Royal Netherlands Marechaussee","https://english.marechaussee.nl/topics/t/temporary-reintroduction-of-border-control"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border controls at Germany’s borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["A temporary reintroduction of border controls are currently in place at Germany’s borders. If you are planning to enter Germany from Netherlands, see information from ",["The Federal Ministry of the Interior and Community","https://www.bmi.bund.de/SharedDocs/pressemitteilungen/EN/2024/09/binnengrenzkontrollen_en.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border controls at Belgium’s borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["Belgium has introduced additional entry checks until December 2025. Checks may be carried out on major roads leading into Belgium, motorway car parks, international bus services, international trains and on intra-Schengen flights. Checks may involve verifying travel documents and identification, as well as screening for illegal substances. In Belgium you must carry your passport with you at all times."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Netherlands guide","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/160/netherlands#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of the Netherlands","https://www.belastingdienst.nl/wps/wcm/connect/bldcontenten/belastingdienst/individuals/abroad_and_customs/restricted_prohibited_import_export/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food and drink into the Netherlands"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into the Netherlands"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is ",["10,000 euros or more","https://www.belastingdienst.nl/wps/wcm/connect/en/customs/content/how-much-money-can-i-take-with-me-while-travelling"],". You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in the Netherlands"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in the Netherlands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. You should remain aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpocketing and bag-snatching are common, particularly in central Amsterdam and around Amsterdam Central Station. Thieves often operate in gangs on the trains and trams to and from Schiphol airport and Central Station. One thief distracts you while another steals your bag. Sleeping on trains can make you an easy target."]},{"k":"p","s":["Thieves enter restaurants on the pretext of selling something or looking for someone. They steal bags while people are distracted."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep sight of your luggage and belongings – especially when checking into hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep valuables securely on your person"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid hanging bags or jackets on the back of a chair in restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid falling asleep in public or on public transport"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fake police scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Amsterdam police have warned of criminals using false police identities to trick tourists into handing over cash and credit cards. They will usually say that it is part of an investigation into counterfeit money or false credit cards. Be very cautious about any approaches."]},{"k":"p","s":["Genuine plain-clothes police will rarely carry out this type of inspection. Dutch police do not have shiny badges, which the fake police sometimes present as ID."]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 0900 8844 to contact the nearest police station if you are unsure whether a police person is genuine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drug sellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid confrontation with anyone offering you drugs. Stay away from quiet or dark alleys, particularly late at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of drink spiking, particularly for young women and solo travellers. Do not leave your drink unattended. If you are in a group, make sure you stay together."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you think your drink has been spiked, seek immediate medical help and contact the police."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Organised crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular incidents of violent crime among organised crime gangs involved in drug trafficking, particularly in Amsterdam, Rotterdam, The Hague, and other large cities. Confrontations between rival gangs have led to violent incidents including shootings, stabbings, and use of homemade explosives."]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk mostly affects those involved in drug crime, but there is always the risk of being in the wrong place at the wrong time. Remain vigilant if you suspect illegal activity. Follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Anyone aged 14 or over must always be able to show identification. British nationals should use their passport as ID. Dual nationals can show a Dutch driving licence, Dutch passport or identity card."]},{"k":"p","s":["For people aged 16 or over who fail to comply with the requirement to identify themselves, the fine is 100 euros. For persons aged 14 and 15, the fine is 50 euros."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Netherlands has a reputation for being tolerant on the use of ‘soft drugs’, such as cannabis. However, drug use is only tolerated in designated premises in the major cities. Buying or possessing prohibited drugs and substances outside of designated areas, including when transiting through airports, is illegal and can result in a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Netherlands have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Smoking soft drugs in public places is illegal. There are specific cafés where it is legal to purchase and use cannabis in limited quantities and under strict conditions."]},{"k":"p","s":["The sale of dry and fresh psychoactive mushrooms is illegal. However, the truffle (sclerotium) form of psychoactive (psilocybin) mushrooms is not covered under Dutch law (Opium Act) and is still sold in regulated ‘smart shops’."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be extremely careful as mixing alcohol, cannabis and wild mushrooms can be fatal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Canal laws and dangers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every year people drown in the canals of Amsterdam and in canals elsewhere in the Netherlands. The majority of drownings happen after heavy drinking or smoking cannabis. Take care when walking beside canals."]},{"k":"p","s":["If police catch you swimming in the Amsterdam canals, they will fine you 160 euros. They will also fine you for urinating in the canals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in the Netherlands, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Netherlands guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/netherlands/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in the Netherlands on a UK driving licence. Always carry your:"]},{"k":"li","s":["driving licence"]},{"k":"li","s":["insurance documents"]},{"k":"li","s":["vehicle documents"]},{"k":"li","s":["photo ID such as a passport or residence permit"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are driving a vehicle that does not belong to you, you may need written permission from the registered owner. You are not allowed to drive on a provisional licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re living in the Netherlands, check the ",["driving requirements for residents","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-the-netherlands"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving regulations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic offences can carry heavy, on-the-spot fines. If you pay a fine, always ask for a receipt."]},{"k":"p","s":["Watch out for trams. They have priority over other traffic. You must stop if a tram or a bus stops in the middle of the road to let passengers on and off."]},{"k":"p","s":["Speed cameras, speed traps and unmarked vehicles are widely used. Motorway speed limits can vary. You must follow overhead illuminated lane indicators when in use."]},{"k":"p","s":["Look out for cyclists and mopeds, who have right of way over motor vehicles and often ignore road traffic rules and red lights."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pedestrian safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be on the look-out for cyclists, mopeds and trams when crossing roads, especially on zebra crossings. If you do not use marked crossings on roads, you could be fined for jaywalking."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cycle paths are busy and cyclists ride at speed."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for the Netherlands","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/160/netherlands#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in the Netherlands","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/160/netherlands"],", including biting insects and ticks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro explains ",["best practice when travelling with medicines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in the Netherlands"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in the Netherlands","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-netherlands-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in the Netherlands, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"li","s":["prescription charges"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in the Netherlands","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-the-netherlands"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in the Netherlands"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=netherlands"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=netherlands"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=netherlands"]," in the Netherlands"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in the Netherlands","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-guide-for-the-netherlands"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in the Netherlands","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/netherlands-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/netherlands/british-embassy-the-hague-netherlands"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/netherlands/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in the Netherlands","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-for-the-netherlands"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":17857,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"9b30edde85e1c26e2b55c4e84d2f3af92ff9d4e9a323e29382de9304953c01b7","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","bytes":80692,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Tanzania travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-30T14:45:53+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to parts of Tanzania"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tanzania"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Tanzania’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Tanzania set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Tanzania High Commission in the UK","https://uk.tzembassy.go.tz/contacts"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Tanzania, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least one blank page."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid British passport or ",["proof of right of abode","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a tourist or business visa to enter Tanzania."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to work or volunteer, you will also need a work permit. Information on how to apply is ",["available from the Tanzanian Prime Minister’s Office","https://epermit.kazi.go.tz/web/main/guidelines"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your employer or volunteer organisation should help you arrange this before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay your visa or permit you can be arrested, detained and fined before being deported."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Tanzanian Immigration Department has ",["more information on visas","https://visa.immigration.go.tz/guidelines"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Apply for an ‘e-visa’","https://visa.immigration.go.tz/"]," before you travel. It is no longer possible to get a visa from the Tanzanian High Commission in London."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also get a tourist or business visa for a single entry on arrival at the ",["main ports of entry to Tanzania","https://immigration.go.tz/index.php/entry-and-exit-point"],", subject to meeting all immigration requirements. You may be asked to provide proof of your return journey. You will not be able to get a multiple entry visa on arrival."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must be ready to show your return or onward ticket at border control."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ebola screening"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 17 October, the ",["Tanzania Ministry of Health","https://www.moh.go.tz/"]," announced heightened health screening measure for travellers from high-risk regions and affected countries, at all points of entry. Further information on countries affected can be found ",["here","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/ebola-and-marburg-haemorrhagic-fevers-outbreaks-and-case-locations#current-incidents-and-outbreaks"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["All travellers are required to fill out the ",["Travellers Health Surveillance Form","https://afyamsafiri.moh.go.tz/#/"]," before departing or on arrival."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mpox screening"]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need to pass through mpox screening, in the form of body temperature checks, at all points of entry into Tanzania."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mandatory travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["All visitors to mainland Tanzania and Zanzibar, except residents, must have mandatory Tanzanian Government-provided inbound travel insurance, even if they already have a personal policy in place. You can buy insurance either online, or at ports of entry upon arrival in both mainland Tanzania and Zanzibar. This insurance is valid for the duration of your stay (up to 92 days)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You only need to buy insurance for your first port of entry, either mainland Tanzania or Zanzibar. You may be refused entry if you do not have the required insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["For travellers who purchase insurance after 1 October:"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you intend to arrive in Zanzibar first, you must buy travel insurance from the Zanzibar Insurance Corporation (ZIC) upon arrival. This can also be purchased online beforehand via ",["visit Zanzibar","https://visitzanzibar.go.tz/"],". If you have questions that are not answered on the website, email ZIC at inbound@zic.co.tz."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive in mainland Tanzania first, you must buy travel insurance from the National Insurance Corporation (NIC) upon arrival. This can also be purchased online beforehand via ",["National Insurance Corporation","https://inbound.nicinsurance.co.tz/apply"],". If you have questions that are not answered on the website, email NIC at wecare.inbound@nicinsurance.co.tz."]},{"k":"p","s":["For travellers who purchased insurance from ZIC before 1 October:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers who purchased travel insurance from ZIC before 1 October may use it where the mainland is their first port of entry, and do not need to purchase travel insurance from NIC."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also make sure you have travel insurance that covers your individual needs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Tanzania, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Tanzania guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/220/tanzania#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Tanzania. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking wildlife products into and out of Tanzania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not bring animal skin accessories into Tanzania as you risk questioning or detention when leaving the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border officials have arrested foreigners for trying to take wildlife items, including horns and seashells, out of the country. It’s illegal to do this without a certified export permit from the Ministry of Natural Resources and Tourism. If you’re caught you could be detained or fined."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Tanzania","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Tanzania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Tanzania cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["embassies"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels"]},{"k":"li","s":["restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["bars"]},{"k":"li","s":["major gatherings like sporting or religious events"]},{"k":"li","s":["crowded places"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Extremists linked to the Islamic terrorist group Al-Shabaab based in Somalia pose a threat across the East Africa region, and are thought to be active in Tanzania. Attacks by IS-Mozambique, who are based in the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, are possible near Tanzania’s border with this area of Mozambique. There is also thought to be some support for Daesh (formerly referred to as ISIL). The Tanzanian authorities have successfully made a number of arrests in connection to terrorism. However, many incidents in Tanzania are of unclear origin and may be conducted by criminal gangs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["A general election took place on 29 October 2025. Protests and the resulting security response led to fatalities and injuries in many areas of mainland Tanzania."]},{"k":"p","s":["Previous elections in Zanzibar have turned violent and resulted in fatalities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Further demonstrations, including violent responses by security forces, are possible at any time. There have been calls on social media for demonstrations to take place on public holidays."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware that there has been an increase in anti-foreigner rhetoric."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay away from all demonstrations, rallies and large crowds, and monitor social media and local media for up-to-date information. If you become aware of any nearby protests or disruption leave the area immediately."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities have previously limited internet access during or after protests. Make a note of important phone numbers including your airline travel operator, insurance company and the FCDO’s consular assistance number in case the internet is not accessible."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take or share photographs and video footage of protests and violence. Keep away from activities that could be considered political, including political discussions in public places or online. There is a risk you could be detained for social media activities including posting comments, blogging or sharing photographs or video footage relating to protests or the current political situation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Electronic Devices"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tanzanian security services may request to check your phone and other electronic devices for content related to the events around elections, and to review participation in online groups perceived to have incited violence. The police have said that it is an offence to hold or share videos or images that ‘cause panic or degrade a person’s dignity’."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of armed crime, including armed robbery, throughout Tanzania. Take particular care in places frequented by tourists and foreign residents. In Dar es Salaam, tourists and residents have been targeted:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the city centre"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the Masaki and Oysterbay peninsula area, particularly at Coco Beach"]},{"k":"li","s":["along Toure Drive"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Zanzibar incidents have taken place in Stone Town and at hotels and on popular tourist beaches throughout the island."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bag snatching is a well-known tactic of criminals, who may operate from cars or motorbikes. If you are walking on the street:"]},{"k":"li","s":["walk towards the traffic so you can see vehicles approaching"]},{"k":"li","s":["walk as far away from the road as possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry bags loosely by the handle or hanging off your shoulder and do not secure the strap across your chest"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking or cycling at night or alone"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not carry large amounts of cash or display valuables such as expensive jewellery or watches. Leave your passport in a safe place and carry a copy for ID checks."]},{"k":"p","s":["When in a vehicle, keep car doors locked, windows up and valuables out of sight. Be particularly careful at night when there is a higher incidence of crime. Do not stop if pedestrians or hitchhikers try to flag you down."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual Assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents of assault, rape and sexual aggression against foreigners have occurred, including at beach resorts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can take steps to reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking alone at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not leave drinks unattended"]},{"k":"li","s":["be wary when dealing with strangers, and anyone offering rides or other invitations"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a victim of a sexual assault or other crime, you can report it to the ",["British High Commission in Dar es Salaam","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-high-commission-dar-es-salaam"],". Consular staff can help:"]},{"k":"li","s":["report the incident with local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["explain the process"]},{"k":"li","s":["translate for you if there’s a language barrier"]},{"k":"p","s":["See FCDO’s guidance for ",["victims of rape and sexual assault in Tanzania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tanzania-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault/tanzania-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Express kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Dar es Salaam, tourists have been ‘express kidnapped’. This means they’ve been assaulted, robbed and forced with the threat of violence to withdraw cash from ATMs. Some have been forced to arrange cash transfers of up to £5,000 through Western Union after being befriended by strangers or getting into unlicensed taxis."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your property"]},{"k":"p","s":["Burglary is a risk, including at hotels and other accommodation. Intruders may try to gain access to rooms. Keep doors and windows locked, especially at night, and use any additional security measures available, such as deadbolts, double locks or security chains."]},{"k":"p","s":["If your accommodation has security staff, ask for identification before allowing anyone you do not know into your room."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Harassment"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been cases where women travelling alone and in small groups have been verbally harassed."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should respect local laws and customs."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are arrested or detained for any reason, you can insist that the British High Commission is notified immediately."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Religion"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high proportion of Muslims in Tanzania, particularly in Zanzibar and Pemba. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions. Make sure your actions do not cause offence, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or if you intend to visit religious areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry copies of your passport photo page and visa. Carry your work permit, if you have one. Immigration officials or police can request these documents at any time, so make sure you can get the originals quickly if you need them. If you’re a resident or longer term visitor, consider getting certified copies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. During this time, avoid eating or drinking in public, outside of hotels or restaurants. Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dress modestly throughout Tanzania. Women wearing shorts or sleeveless tops away from tourist resorts in Zanzibar and Pemba, particularly in Stone Town, may cause offence to the local population."]},{"k":"p","s":["Zanzibari authorities can fine you 700 US dollars or more if you’re wearing what they consider inappropriate clothing in public. For guides or tour operators, the fine can be at least 1,000 US dollars."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Environmental laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Plastic bags are banned for environmental reasons. If you arrive by air you’ll be asked to hand over all plastic bags on arrival. The ban does not include ‘ziplock’ bags for airline security procedures."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tanzania has strict laws on drug use. There may be severe penalties, including lengthy prison sentences which can be applied both for supplying and simple possession of any drugs, including when transiting through the airport. Some ‘herbal highs’ and products containing cannabidiol (CBD) are illegal in Tanzania. Travellers are advised to ensure they do not try to enter Tanzania with skincare products and e-cigarette refills containing CBD. Penalties for importing and trafficking controlled substances can be severe, including up to 30 years’ imprisonment in some cases."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Tanzania have technology and security for detecting illegal items, including cannabis. This can be used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tanzanian prisons tend to be dirty and overcrowded."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Discrimination and harassment"]},{"k":"p","s":["Reports made to the British High Commission by Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic (BAME) British passport holders suggest that they are experiencing additional levels of harassment from immigration officials. If this happens, stay calm and ask that the ",["British High Commission","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-high-commission-dar-es-salaam"]," is immediately informed."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Tanzania, including Zanzibar. Same-sex relationships are not tolerated in Tanzania’s conservative society. If you show affection in public, like holding hands or kissing in public places, you could be arrested or put in prison."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["US dollars are widely accepted in tourist areas. Travellers cheques are not widely accepted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most banks in major cities have ATMs that accept foreign debit cards and issue Tanzanian shillings. They sometimes break down or run out of money."]},{"k":"p","s":["Widespread cash shortages were reported in the days of political unrest that followed the 29 October 2025 election."]},{"k":"p","s":["To minimise the risk of card cloning, use ATMs located within the bank. If you try to exchange non-Bank of England pound notes, you may get a reduced exchange rate."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Game reserves and national parks"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting game reserves and national parks, always follow park regulations and advice from wardens."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only use reputable tour operators. Do not buy safari tours from touts. The Tanzanian Association of Tour Operators (TATO) ",["TATO – Tanzania Association of Tour Operators – Tour Operators Association of Tanzania (tatotz.org)","https://www.tatotz.org/"]," maintains a list of licensed tour companies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Trekking and climbing"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are trekking or climbing, only use a reputable travel company, stick to established routes and always walk in groups. Make sure you are well prepared and equipped to cope with the terrain and low temperatures."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List (ASL)","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list#tanzania"]," lists all airlines certified by the authorities with responsibility for regulatory oversight of Tanzania. These airlines are banned from operating commercial air services to, from, and within the United Kingdom. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive in Tanzania, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The condition of cars rented out by some car hire companies is variable, so use a reputable firm. There are no roadside rescue or breakdown services. Road maps are hard to come by and not always up to date. Service stations are infrequent and may not have supplies of fuel. Consider using reputable taxis as an alternative."]},{"k":"p","s":["Widespread fuel shortages were reported in the days of political unrest that followed the 29 October 2025 election."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive in Tanzania with a UK driving licence for up to 6 months. For stays longer than this, an international driving permit (IDP) is required. Keep this with you in the car. To confirm the correct IDP to use, contact the ",["Tanzanian High Commission in the UK","https://www.uk.tzembassy.go.tz/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["To drive in Zanzibar, you’ll also need a local Zanzibar driving permit (which you can get through your hire car company). Carry several copies of your driving licence, permits and insurance documents."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards and road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road users often drive dangerously, ignoring the rules of the road. Accidents resulting in death and serious injury are common."]},{"k":"p","s":["Watch out for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["vehicles and motorbikes trying to undertake or overtake using any lane, including on the hard shoulder"]},{"k":"li","s":["drivers making manoeuvres without signalling"]},{"k":"li","s":["poor attention to rules at roundabouts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many roads need repair, including in major towns and cities. During the rainy season, flooding can cause landslides and road surfaces can deteriorate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads in Tanzania’s national parks, mainly dirt tracks, can become hazardous or impassable after heavy rain. It may be essential to have a 4-wheel drive vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid driving outside major towns and cities at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Police checkpoints"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent police checkpoints. If you’re stopped by the police, ask to see identification. If you are issued with a fine, the police should give you a government control number for payment. The police should not ask you to make any on the spot payments for traffic violations. If you’re involved in a road accident, co-operate with the local police."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you see an unusual incident, or if somebody in plain clothes tries to flag you down, it is often safer not to stop."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buses and taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Local buses (‘dala dalas’), motorbike taxis (‘boda bodas’), and tuk-tuks (known locally as ‘bijajis’) can have poor safety standards. They are often poorly maintained and badly driven. They rarely have proper insurance cover. There are frequent accidents, some of which result in fatalities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not accept lifts from strangers or anyone offering to find a taxi for you. It is safest to arrange a taxi through a hotel or travel operator. Always ask to see the driver’s ID and use reputable taxi services."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpockets and bag-snatchers operate on overcrowded buses and at bus stations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several accidents on Tanzanian railways. Seek local advice for any long-distance train travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lake and sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["In the last few years there have been several ferry disasters. Hundreds of people have died when travelling:"]},{"k":"li","s":["between Dar es Salaam and Zanzibar"]},{"k":"li","s":["between the islands of Zanzibar"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the Lake Zone area"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you think a ferry is overloaded or not seaworthy, do not get on. If you do board, familiarise yourself with emergency procedures on board and make a note of where the life jackets and emergency exits are located."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also beware of aggressive ticket touts at Tanzanian ports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Continual pirate attacks on vessels sailing off the coast of Somalia and in the Gulf of Aden show that the threat of piracy remains significant. The threat assessment of the combined international naval counter-piracy forces is that all sailing yachts under their own passage should avoid the ",["designated high-risk area","https://on-shore.mschoa.org/"]," or accept the risk of being hijacked and held hostage for ransom. For more information and advice, see ",["Piracy and armed robbery at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rainy seasons"]},{"k":"p","s":["The length of rainy seasons can vary, but they generally run from:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the end of March to May"]},{"k":"li","s":["October to mid-December"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rainfall and strong winds can affect travel. Flooding and landslides can occur during heavy rain. If travelling to affected regions, you should take extra care and follow any advice given by the local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local and international weather reports and the ",["TMA website","https://www.meteo.go.tz/"]," for the latest updates. If travelling, plan your journeys carefully and make sure to follow local guidance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid walking, swimming, or driving through floodwater."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes and tremors are a risk in Tanzania. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The last significant earthquake (magnitude 6.0) happened on 12 August 2020, 66km north-east of Mafia Island."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires can occur during periods of hot and dry weather, including in Kilimanjaro National Park. If you are affected by a wildfire, contact your tour operator and follow the instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you see a wildfire, move to a safe location away from vegetation and smoke. If sheltering in a building or vehicle, assess whether it is safe to remain there and keep windows and vents closed. If you require specific information about an upcoming trip, you are advised to contact your tour operator."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Tanzania. It only covers regions where The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read FCDO’s ",["overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mtwara Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to any area within 20km of the Tanzanian border with the Cabo Delgado province of Mozambique, due to attacks by groups linked with Islamic extremism."]},{"k":"p","s":["The presence of groups linked to Islamic extremism in Cabo Delgado is creating cross-border tensions and instability. There is a risk of violent attacks. An attack on Kitaya village in October 2020 was claimed by groups linked to Islamic extremism operating from northern Mozambique."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tanzania-Burundi border and Kigoma region"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been armed robberies in the area bordering Burundi and in Kigoma region, including vehicle hijackings. Drive only in hours of daylight. There are few facilities for visitors."]},{"k":"h","s":["National parks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some parks are extremely remote, and emergency access and evacuation can be difficult. If you choose to camp, only use official sites. Make sure you are properly equipped and seek local advice when travelling to isolated areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are risks associated with viewing wildlife, particularly on foot or at close range. Always follow park regulations and advice from wardens, and make sure you have the correct documentation or permit before entering a national park."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Tanzania","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/220/tanzania#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Tanzania","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/220/tanzania"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["cholera"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Tanzania. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Tanzania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities are limited, especially outside Dar es Salaam."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Tanzania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilities-in-tanzania"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Tanzania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Tanzania"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Tanzania"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Tanzania"]," in Tanzania"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Tanzania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tanzania-bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Tanzania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tanzania-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/tanzania/british-high-commission-dar-es-salaam"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Tanzania","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-for-tanzania"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":27138,"change":"Additional information about use of security measures to reduce the risk of burglary in hotels and other accommodation (‘Safety and security’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/nato-witnesses-a-surge-of-airspace-violations-by-russia-as-moscow-seeks-to-test-alliance-297361":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T23:33Z","sha":"4c324afa5fdbff30364a1b5765750739de39afc0129006dba9897167a1944454","read":"https://theconversation.com/nato-witnesses-a-surge-of-airspace-violations-by-russia-as-moscow-seeks-to-test-alliance-297361","bytes":184286,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"NATO witnesses a surge of airspace violations by Russia as Moscow seeks to test alliance","by":[{"n":"Frederic Lemieux","r":"Professor of the Practice and Faculty Director of the Master's in Applied Intelligence, Georgetown University"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T22:52:03Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["NATO convened an ",["urgent meeting on Nov. 23, 2026","https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/11/23/nato-calls-urgent-meeting-string-incidents-escalates-russia-tensions/"],", to discuss the violation of members’ airspace by Russia."]},{"k":"p","s":["It follows an incident three days earlier in which three objects – believed to be two missiles and a drone – crashed in Poland in what the country’s prime minister, Donald Tusk, described as an ",["“intentional provocation” by Russia","https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/polish-army-investigates-report-unknown-objects-near-ukraine-border-2026-11-20/"],". If true, it would be far from the first such testing of the airspace of a NATO country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Russian aircraft, drones and missiles have violated NATO airspace dozens of times since the full-scale invasion of Ukraine began in February 2022. And while individually, many of these incidents appear minor – a drone crash here, a brief fighter incursion there, a missile discovered only after the fact – taken together, I believe the numbers tell a far more troubling story."]},{"k":"p","s":["To get a full picture of the scale of violations, ",["I conducted","https://scs.georgetown.edu/faculty/4121170/frederic-lemieux"]," a systematic review of Russian airspace violations against NATO members) from 2022 through the end of November."]},{"k":"p","s":["It reveals not just an increase but a sharp acceleration accompanied by rising severity and widening geographic scope. In 2026, through Nov. 20, NATO members recorded 25 attributed Russian airspace violations – more than four times as many as in 2024 and 43% of all incidents recorded over the five-year period."]},{"k":"p","s":["This has not been a gradual escalation; it was a dramatic change."]},{"k":"h","s":["Picking up pace"]},{"k":"p","s":["I identified airspace violations through a systematic review of international news media coverage, corroborated with official NATO press releases and cross-validated against operational assessments and geospatial reporting from the ",["Institute for the Study of War","https://understandingwar.org/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Included were violations of airspace by drones heavily suspected to be Russian but that could not be 100% confirmed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Between 2022 and 2024, the annual number of violations rose steadily but modestly. There were four incidents in 2022, five in 2023 and six in 2024. That corresponds to year-on-year increases of roughly 25% and 20%."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2025, the count jumped to 18, a 200% increase in a single year. And that pace has continued into 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such a surge is statistically and strategically significant. It strongly suggests that Russian airspace violations are no longer episodic spillovers from the war in Ukraine, but part of a sustained pattern of pressure directed at NATO itself. The 2026 figures reinforce this: The count has kept rising even after the 2025 surge."]},{"k":"p","s":["The character of these incidents has also changed."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022, all four violations were what I classify as low-intensity events: brief incursions into Swedish airspace by Russian fighters, the crash of an Orlan-10 reconnaissance drone in Romania and the later discovery of a Russian cruise missile in Poland. These incidents were serious but short-lived and geographically limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["By 2023, violations had become more repetitive. Romania alone ",["experienced multiple drone incursions","https://www.rferl.org/a/romania-ukraine-russia-drone-fire-overhead-civilian-danube-delta/33605410.html"]," and debris discoveries over several months, often triggering fighter scrambles. All five incidents that year fell into a midrange severity category: more persistent than before but still largely confined to border regions."]},{"k":"p","s":["The transition toward higher-intensity incursions became clearer in 2024. Of the six violations that year, half involved high-severity characteristics such as deeper penetration of a NATO country or broader geographic exposure. A Russian cruise missile ",["crossed into Polish airspace","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/poland-says-russian-missile-entered-its-airspace-during-latest-major-attack-on-ukraine"],", drones ",["entered Romania","https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/ukraine-destroys-25-38-drones-russian-attack-air-force-says-2024-07-25/"]," on multiple consecutive nights, and a Russian drone ",["crashed well inside Latvian territory","https://www.twz.com/air/russian-shahed-kamikaze-drone-crashes-in-latvia"],". These incidents expanded both the depth and the geographic footprint of violations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then came 2025. Of the 18 violations recorded that year, a clear majority qualify as high-severity events. These include a Russian drone that ",["penetrated nearly 60 miles (100 kilometers)","https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/ukraine-says-russia-drone-incursion-part-pressure-plan-against-west-2025-09-26/"]," into Polish territory before crashing near Osiny without prior radar detection; a drone that ",["remained inside Romanian airspace","https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20250913-romania-says-a-drone-breached-its-airspace-during-russian-strikes-on-ukraine"]," for approximately four hours, crossing multiple counties before crashing in Vaslui; and a ",["massive 21-drone swarm over Poland","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/10/poland-downs-drones-during-airspace-intrusion-as-russia-strikes-ukraine"]," on Sept. 9-10 that forced the closure of major civilian airports in Warsaw, Rzeszów and Lublin."]},{"k":"p","s":["Manned aircraft also returned in force. Russian MiG-31 interceptors ",["flew over Estonia for about 12 minutes","https://estonianworld.com/security/chart-shows-russian-jets-12-minute-violation-of-estonian-airspace/"]," with transponders – onboard devices that automatically respond to radar signals by transmitting an aircraft’s identity and altitude, enabling air traffic control and air defense systems to track it – switched off."]},{"k":"p","s":["In October, a Russian Su-30 fighter accompanied by an Il-78 refueling tanker ",["violated Lithuanian airspace","https://www.dw.com/en/russian-military-aircraft-enter-airspace-of-nato-member-lithuania/a-74477897"]," – an unmistakable signal of endurance and deliberate mission planning."]},{"k":"p","s":["In December 2025, suspected ",["Russian drones were shot down and later recovered","https://www.hurriyetdailynews.com/amp/drone-found-on-black-sea-coast-likely-russian-officials-say-218885"]," in Turkey on multiple dates, indicating a persistent provocation rather than a one-off incursion."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perhaps most strikingly, Western Europe was seemingly no longer exempt. On Dec. 4, 2025, five unidentified drones ",["flew over France’s Île Longue naval base","https://www.thetimes.com/world/europe/article/france-shoots-down-suspected-russian-drones-nuclear-sub-base-dz7x3qzcz"],", home to the country’s nuclear ballistic missile submarines. French personnel reportedly fired at the suspected Russian drones."]},{"k":"p","s":["Just weeks later, on Christmas Day, ",["Polish fighters intercepted a Russian reconnaissance aircraft","https://www.dw.com/en/polish-jets-intercept-russian-spy-plane/a-75307011"]," over the Baltic Sea."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2026, the incidents grew more dangerous. In May, a Russian drone ",["struck an apartment block in Galați, Romania","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c93x4nxlkjeo"],", injuring two people, the first civilian injuries on NATO soil from such an incursion. Then on July 30, a Russian Kh-101 cruise missile ",["flew roughly 60 miles (100 kilometers) into Poland","https://aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/31/poland-protests-to-russian-ambassador-over-missile-incursion"]," before exploding in a field near Lublin. On Nov. 20, during a mass Russian strike on Ukraine, a Kh-101, likely a second missile and a jet-powered drone ",["entered Polish airspace","https://www.rte.ie/news/2026/1120/1600008-poland-russia-airspace-violations/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Manned aircraft also crossed into NATO airspace. A Russian Su-30 fighter ",["entered Estonian airspace","https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2026-03-19/estonia-summons-russian-diplomat-after-russian-jet-violates-estonian-airspace"]," in March with no flight plan and no contact with air traffic control, and in September, a Russian Mi-8 helicopter ",["crossed from Kaliningrad into Poland","https://notesfrompoland.com/2026/09/23/russian-military-helicopter-violates-polish-airspace/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Gray-zone tactics"]},{"k":"p","s":["Severity and frequency are not the only dimensions that changed. Geographical reach has, too. In 2022, Russian violations affected three NATO members. By 2024, that number had grown to four. In 2025, it expanded to six: Romania, Poland, Estonia, Lithuania, Turkey and France. In 2026, the violations attributed to Russia have so far been concentrated in four members – Romania, Poland, Estonia and Lithuania – with Romania alone accounting for 20 of the 25. Romania’s defense ministry ",["counted 35 unauthorized drone entries","https://www.stripes.com/theaters/europe/2026-10-19/romania-drones-nato-meeting-23196504.html"]," by mid-October, many too brief to be reported individually."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pressure was applied simultaneously in the Black Sea region, the Baltic states and Western Europe."]},{"k":"p","s":["This widening scope matters because it undermines the idea that these incidents are localized accidents. Instead, they resemble a distributed pattern of Russia probing across NATO’s eastern and southern flanks and into its strategic core. The narrower footprint in 2026 does not signal de-escalation. The pressure has instead concentrated along the flank that borders the war, and it has grown more dangerous there. NATO’s political response reflects this shift. For the first time since the war began, members invoked ",["Article 4 of the North Atlantic Treaty","https://www.cnn.com/2025/09/11/europe/nato-article-four-poland-drones-intl"],", the mechanism for collective consultation when a member feels its security is threatened."]},{"k":"p","s":["Poland ",["did so","https://www.npr.org/2025/09/10/nx-s1-5536649/russian-drones-crossed-into-their-airspace-so-poland-invoked-article-4-what-is-it"]," after the September 2025 drone swarm, and ",["Estonia followed","https://apnews.com/article/nato-article-4-explainer-russia-poland-estonia-26415920dfb8458725bda517337adb12"]," after the MiG-31 incursion later that month. Although only two of the 18 incidents triggered Article 4, their timing is revealing: No such invocations occurred in the previous three years combined."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2026, no member has invoked Article 4 so far, even after a Russian cruise missile flew deep into Poland in July. Instead, allies have shifted from tolerance to engagement: Romanian F-16s and allied jets have ",["shot down six Russian drones over Romania","https://militarnyi.com/en/news/romanian-f-16s-shoot-down-two-drones-that-entered-the-country-s-airspace/"],", and Italian Eurofighters ",["destroyed an armed Russian drone over Lithuania","https://www.euronews.com/2026/09/15/nato-committed-and-ready-after-shooting-down-drone-over-lithuania"]," in September."]},{"k":"p","s":["From a strategic standpoint, the danger lies less in any single violation than in their cumulative effect. Airspace incursions ",["sit in a gray zone","https://www.rusi.org/explore-our-research/publications/commentary/deterring-kremlin-grey-zone-aggression-against-nato"]," between peace and open conflict. They impose operational and psychological costs, test air defense systems and provide valuable intelligence on NATO’s detection thresholds and response times, all while staying below the legal threshold of armed attack."]},{"k":"h","s":["Testing NATO’s resolve"]},{"k":"p","s":["The data from 2025 and 2026 shows that this gray-zone activity has intensified dramatically. A threefold increase in 2025, followed by a further rise in 2026, coupled with a shift toward deeper, longer and more disruptive incidents across multiple theaters, points to a deliberate campaign rather than accidental spillover."]},{"k":"p","s":["For NATO, the implication is clear. Monitoring individual incidents is no longer sufficient. What now matters is the rate of acceleration, the severity profile and the geographic dispersion of violations. If current trends persist as the war in Ukraine enters its fifth year, the alliance’s greatest challenge may not be responding to a single dramatic breach but managing the mounting pressure created by many smaller ones – each calibrated to test resolve without triggering open conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is an updated version of an ",["article originally published by The Conversation","https://theconversation.com/russia-tested-natos-airspace-18-times-in-2025-alone-a-200-surge-that-signals-a-dangerous-shift-273318"]," on Feb. 19, 2026."]}],"chars":9187},"https://theconversation.com/andy-burnhams-brussels-deal-throws-up-a-paradox-for-both-sides-in-the-eu-debate-297589":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-26T15:06Z","sha":"2aa6dca1edb3e3cb88d1ecce9e42e3b97fde60e69905d58b53f55192724a5c0e","read":"https://theconversation.com/andy-burnhams-brussels-deal-throws-up-a-paradox-for-both-sides-in-the-eu-debate-297589","bytes":178325,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Andy Burnham’s Brussels deal throws up a paradox for both sides in the EU debate","by":[{"n":"Benjamin Martill","r":"Senior Lecturer in Politics and International Relations, University of Edinburgh"}],"pub":"2026-11-26T13:58:48Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["At a summit in Brussels this month, UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham revealed breakthroughs in the UK-EU “reset” begun under his predecessor Keir Starmer."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["summit","https://theconversation.com/topics/european-union-eu-539"]," produced agreement on ",["several important issues","https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2026/11/20/joint-statement-eu-united-kingdom-summit-20-november-2026/"],". New rules from March 2028 will remove the need for certification of animal and food products, UK and EU emissions trading systems (ETS) will be linked, and a youth experience scheme will enable up to 100,000 18 to 31-year-olds to work and study in the UK or EU."]},{"k":"p","s":["And in the meantime, both sides reaffirmed their commitment to working towards a closer relationship."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet the announcement came in for criticism from the political right. Conservative leader Kemi Badenoch ",["argued","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6vg2v9xkr40o"]," that Burnham had “oversold” the deal when he presented it to parliament. She said the prime minister was trying to take Britain “back to 2015”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, Reform UK’s leader Nigel Farage ",["claimed","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CQKGTNco_AM"]," the agreement amounted to a betrayal of Brexit."]},{"k":"h","s":["A lightning rod for criticism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Notably, the reset appears to be garnering more intense criticism than it did under Starmer. One reason for this is that the stakes are now higher. Burnham has already sought to shift the dial on Europe and has openly flirted with the possibility of the UK rejoining the EU."]},{"k":"p","s":["Both sides see the summit an opportunity to lay the groundwork for the bigger fight to come."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criticism of the deal is already having a chilling effect. Burnham has been noticeably more coy in his language about rejoining the EU, insisting ",["in his remarks","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/c65y195llkvyt"]," to the House of Commons that he would seek to rejoin only if it was in the UK’s interests – and on the back of a new referendum."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the criticism from the Conservatives and Reform of the reset announcement misses the point. What it actually does is highlight the limitations of being outside the EU."]},{"k":"p","s":["Badenoch’s claim that Burnham oversold the deal partly reflects the numbers involved, which look small but are in fact significant. The ",["promised 0.4% increase in GDP","https://lordslibrary.parliament.uk/uk-eu-summit-and-options-for-developing-a-closer-uk-eu-relationship/"]," amounts to a significant economic boost at a time when UK growth has been sluggish. This is hardly trivial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, the non-EU trade deals preferred by Reform and the Conservatives have resulted in a far smaller contributon to UK growth than Burnham’s reset deal. UK accession to the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), for instance, is associated with an anticipated boost to GDP just ",["one tenth","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2023/nov/25/uks-flagship-post-brexit-trade-deal-worth-even-less-than-previously-thought-obr-says"]," the size of the current reset."]},{"k":"p","s":["And yes, Badenoch may be right that the figure is not going to change the world. But this reflects the limitations imposed by Brexit more than anything else."]},{"k":"p","s":["Back in 2016, the Leave campaign claimed that withdrawing from the EU would not disproportionately ",["affect the trading relationship","https://digital.library.lse.ac.uk/Documents/Detail/the-choice/125764"]," with the bloc. That turned out to be illusory, as the EU correctly surmised that affording the UK special treatment would undermine the value of membership and lead to the ",["disintegration of the internal market","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13501763.2020.1810103"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Thus, the EU has ",["opposed efforts by the UK","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/government-and-opposition/article/collective-power-europe-the-government-and-oppositionleonard-schapiro-lecture-2022/B96925F3BC6D45517AC253D1F0AEB44C"]," to negotiate piecemeal integration into the single market – which it describes as “cherry picking”. Perhaps unsurprisingly, it has only been willing to negotiate on specific areas where it sees a discernible benefit for the bloc."]},{"k":"p","s":["The real limitation of Burnham’s deal is not a lack of ambition, but the strictures imposed by Brexit. And getting that 0.4% figure up would mean being open to more radical forms of re-engagement – as Burnham is indeed doing. (Estimates of the ",["economic benefits","https://www.europeanmovement.co.uk/uk_rejoining_eu_explained"]," of rejoining the EU are between 4%-6% of GDP)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Badenoch also notes, correctly, that the deal requires the UK to align with EU rules. But again, this is a symptom of Brexit, which removed the UK from EU decision-making forums and from any say over these rules. Since Brexit, the UK has continued to mimic EU rules in many areas – including ",["state aid","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/13501763.2023.2208684"]," – without having any influence over them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Solving the UK’s rule-taker problem arguably points to the benefits of rejoining. This would return the UK’s place within the EU’s legislative process and solve the so-called ",["“democratic deficit”","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/jcms.13421"]," afflicting third-party countries participating in the internal market."]},{"k":"p","s":["The simultaneous conversations on the reset and rejoining the EU result in a paradox for both sides. For the right, criticising Burnham’s agreement offers a means of heading off further moves towards the EU. But it also highlights the very real limitations of what is possible outside that framework."]},{"k":"p","s":["And for Burnham and Labour europhiles, the need to tout the agreement as a success misses a clear opportunity to highlight the limits of Brexit and the benefits of rejoining."]},{"k":"p","s":["Both sides, in their own way, miss what the reset really makes clear. That is that the deal exposes the continued trade-offs of Brexit and the limits of what is possible outside the EU."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hence the political right may inadvertently bolster the case for rejoining – while Labour proudly showcases what can be achieved from the outside."]}],"chars":4908},"https://theconversation.com/how-the-fall-of-the-berlin-wall-shapes-the-way-germans-vote-today-296018":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-27T11:21Z","sha":"6372147f96093d312ee193d12f2166435c5f05ffa6f7f828f4c9a0c475ca0dd8","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-the-fall-of-the-berlin-wall-shapes-the-way-germans-vote-today-296018","bytes":178871,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How the fall of the Berlin Wall shapes the way Germans vote today","by":[{"n":"Christiane Bertram","r":"Research Scientist at the Hector Research Institute of Education Sciences and Psychology, University of Tübingen"}],"pub":"2026-11-26T15:20:35Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Germany’s far right is on the rise, with current polls suggesting the Alternative für Deutschland (AfD) has the backing of 28% of voters nationally. This makes it the most popular party in the country, ahead of German chancellor Friedrich Merz’s Christian Democrats at 20%."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, there are geographical divides in the AfD’s support. Polling ",["indicates","https://dawum.de/AfD/"]," that over 35% of voters in east ",["Germany","https://theconversation.com/topics/germany-1289"]," support the AfD compared with 20% in the west. My ",["research","https://kops.uni-konstanz.de/server/api/core/bitstreams/9884e81a-9d17-4463-9911-9664f182ba48/content"]," offers insights into why, 36 years after Germany was reunified, there are differences in voting behaviour between both sides of the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2019, two video artists, advised by me and other researchers and historians, ",["interviewed 26 people","https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/293481"]," about their lives in a divided and reunified Germany. These people were all born in 1975 and grew up in different areas of the country: east or west Berlin, Baden-Württemberg in the south-west or Brandenburg in the north-east."]},{"k":"p","s":["My ",["analysis","https://www.hep-verlag.ch/geschichtslernen-in-zeiten-der-krise"]," of the interviews found that west Germans consistently stated their lives had not changed as a result of reunification. Torsten*, an interviewee from Baden-Württemberg, said: “For me, everything was fine before and everything is still fine.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["On the other hand, all of the east German interviewees experienced the transition from the planned-economy socialism of the German Democratic Republic to the social market economy of the Federal Republic of Germany as a profound change."]},{"k":"p","s":["As 14-year-olds at the time of reunification, their entire lives were turned upside down. Nathalie, who grew up in east Berlin, where she still lives, said: “That’s when the chaos began, I’d say. My nice, orderly world just wasn’t so orderly anymore. I felt like I’d lost my footing.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Reunification did present opportunities for east Germans, including greater freedom in choosing a career and new chances to travel. When asked what changes the fall of the Berlin Wall had brought about, Matthias from Brandenburg explained: “For me, that was the biggest opportunity of my life. I don’t know where I’d be now if that turning point hadn’t happened the way it did.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["But people like Matthias also had to witness businesses from former East Germany struggle to withstand new economic competition. The closure of unprofitable firms and the massive job cuts in companies that were sold, primarily to west German investors, meant they saw their parents and grandparents lose their jobs and towns and neighbourhoods left desolate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some of the interviewees spoke of a feeling of “devaluation” and of being treated as second-class citizens. Matthias recalled travelling to West Germany on a student exchange programme and hearing the parents of host students ask whether teenagers from the east knew how to eat with a knife and fork."]},{"k":"p","s":["The majority of the west German interviewees knew little about the German Democratic Republic era and the challenges associated with the fall of the Berlin Wall. And many were unaware that inequalities between the two sides of the country persist."]},{"k":"p","s":["These include the fact that ",["less wealth","https://www.deutschland.de/en/topic/politics/eastern-germany-economy-disadvantage-afd"]," is passed down through the generations in eastern Germany and that a higher share of households in western Germany ",["own their homes","https://www.destatis.de/EN/Themes/Society-Environment/Income-Consumption-Living-Conditions/Assets-Debts/Tables/household-owning-real-proberty-evs.html"]," than in the east. West Germans also ",["occupy a large share","https://www.dw.com/en/study-shows-germanys-east-west-divide-in-top-positions/a-66875990"]," of top positions in east German companies."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a result, the west German interviewees did not understand the dissatisfaction felt by many in the east. Elke, from Baden-Württemberg, said in reference to east German complaints: “Man, you’ve been here for so long now. Why are you complaining? You’ve built such a great life for yourself here, and you’ve been given so many opportunities.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["For east Germans, on the other hand, the effects of inequality are part of everyday life. The people interviewed as part of the project had come to terms with the fact they are not listened to and that no understanding is shown towards them."]},{"k":"h","s":["Bridging the divide"]},{"k":"p","s":["This feeling of not being heard or understood could be a leading factor in why many people in eastern Germany are ",["voting for the AfD","https://theconversation.com/germany-why-the-afd-won-in-saxony-anhalt-and-what-happens-next-291309"],". The party is promising radical change and, in eastern regions, ",["promotes nostalgia","https://www.politico.eu/article/germany-far-right-taps-nostalgia-communist-east-election-campaign/"]," for the German Democratic Republic era."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to a ",["national survey","https://www.ndr.de/ndrfragt/umfrage-mehrheit-sieht-ost-und-west-noch-nicht-als-einheit,deutsche-einheit-168.html"]," released after the Saxony-Anhalt regional election in September, where the AfD secured victory with 43.8% of the vote, many east Germans see economic disparities and a lack of recognition for their achievements as an obstacle to national unity."]},{"k":"p","s":["That is why it is important for east and west Germans to talk to one another, helping them come to terms with the past and shape the present together. This is the aim of outreach projects I run with my colleagues."]},{"k":"p","s":["In one of these projects, ",["Connecting Generations","https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/285195"],", we present video installations based in part on a selection of our interviews with the Germans born in 1975. We display the video installations in public spaces such as museums, memorial sites, libraries and adult education centres throughout Germany."]},{"k":"p","s":["The aim is to provide Germans with spaces for encounter and dialogue. West Germans learn about the history of division and the period of change, and can familiarise themselves with the perspectives of people from the east."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another project, ",["Generations in Dialogue","https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/295026"],", focused on schools. We presented a video installation partly based on the same interviews and invited eyewitnesses into school classes to talk about their experiences."]},{"k":"p","s":["After all, greater knowledge and understanding of all perspectives are needed to bridge the political divide between east and west Germany."]},{"k":"p","s":["*The names of the interviewees have been changed to protect their anonymity."]}],"chars":5538}};
